('de39b31a-d660-485d-ad57-73e9b4b85232', 'Curl (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '4471201', '04471201-EZ-Barbell-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'EZ Curl', 'EZ Curl', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('de3c3a63-b29d-4d2a-ad79-3679fddc6dc2', 'Standing Serratus Push (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The standing position engages your core for stability. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '92011201', '92011201-Resitance-Band-Standing-Serratus-Push-(female)_Che.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resitance Band Standing Serratus Push. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'serratus', 'Standing Serratus Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('de408513-df3b-4969-8f16-5b17e465a44e', 'Chin To Chest Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stretching movement that works your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '45091201', '45091201-Chin-to-chest-Stretch-(male)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Chin To Chest Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Chin To Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('de440bf6-0379-4ab7-90ea-0b47ac847a55', 'Concentration Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '23721201', '23721201-Dumbbell-Concentration-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Concentration Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Concentration Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('de4e2344-99b6-4141-a928-b72a3c350677', 'Back Bend Over Bench Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '94641201', '94641201-Back-Bend-Over-Bench-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Back Bend Over Bench Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Back Bend Over Bench Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('de67cab2-799f-4159-9f56-775b4dfa4c42', 'Lying Bent Leg Raise - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '67191201', '67191201-Lying-Alternate-Bent-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternate Bent Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Bent Leg Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('de75a03e-f0d1-4085-811c-63c28b1a4829', 'Angled Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this pressing movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '88151201', '88151201-Lever-Angled-Leg-Press-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Angled Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Angled Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('de7b58be-5ac0-460b-be50-dd9661cb8fd2', 'Bent Press (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your abs with the Kettlebell Bent Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '26541201', '26541201-Kettlebell-Bent-Press-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Bent Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bent Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('de9990e6-e68a-41de-b272-9f80a7226302', 'Bicep Curl (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Machine', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '43361201', '43361201-Lever-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lever Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('de9cf026-5a70-44a1-8d65-f32b71494cfc', 'Seated Single Leg Raise (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Single Leg Raise On Chair is a lower body raising exercise that targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '87431201', '87431201-Seated-Single-Leg-Raise-on-Chair-(male)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Single Leg Raise On Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dea0da26-e0ab-4957-a612-bca8cfd3384f', 'Repeated Small Jumps', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic jumping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '94081201', '94081201-Repeated-Small-Jumps-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Repeated Small Jumps. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Repeated Small Jumps', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
