('deb337f2-64cf-459e-ba28-261cb86e5ac8', 'Wide Bench Air Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '93231201', '93231201-Wide-Bench-Air-Squat-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Wide Bench Air Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('deb91860-b8b5-437b-bf42-368ecc6bf2a5', 'Seated Figure Four Rock', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your glutes, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your hips work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '95311201', '95311201-Sitting-Figure-Four-Rock-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Figure Four Rock. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Seated Figure Four Rock', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('debdb5c4-bd65-4826-96f3-e9f96264b379', 'Crunch Hold With Legs On Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Crunch Hold With Legs On Bench, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '43321201', '43321201-Crunch-Hold-with-Legs-on-Bench_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch Hold With Legs On Bench', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('deccd703-fa58-43b8-90c6-c579b5edca14', 'Pull Up - Reverse Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Reverse Grip Pull Up is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '6741201', '06741201-Reverse-grip-Pull-up_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Pull Up - Reverse Grip', 'Pull Up - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('decf8d36-f02a-4b74-9c73-dc71996ebe83', 'Lateral Shuffle Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lateral Shuffle Crunches is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic crunching movements. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '78271201', '78271201-Lateral-Shuffle-Crunches-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Lateral Shuffle Crunch', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dedb3280-f2ad-46b7-a4a2-902b66c5cdbc', 'Landmine Sissy Squat (Landmine)', 'Legs', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '83411201', '83411201-Landmine-Sissy-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Landmine Sissy Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('dedc2eca-2015-4f06-9103-51eb225188c9', '45 Degree Twisting Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '73671201', '73671201-45-degree-Twisting-Hyperextension-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Hip Hinge / Trunk Extension', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degree Twisting Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dedd379c-cd32-4bc7-85c8-02d0ac2eee5c', 'Hip Thrust On Knees (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '72771201', '72771201-Resistance-Band-Hip-Thrusts-on-Knees-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Hip Thrusts On Knees. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Hip Thrust On Knees', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('dedf7390-5ee2-4e74-88c7-66ff61b29a3e', 'Rear Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Dumbbell Rear Fly, an effective shoulder flying exercise. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '3781201', '03781201-Dumbbell-Rear-Fly_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Rear Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('defa13ed-2d5b-4609-b3d7-0b0e84a58e73', 'Starfish Crunch (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Dumbbell Starfish Crunch, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54641201', '54641201-Dumbbell-Starfish-Crunch-(beginner)-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Starfish Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Starfish Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('defd9fce-5c3c-4bd6-9e2e-b66c951249f1', 'Overhead Triceps Extension Straight Bar (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Overhead Triceps Extension Straight Bar targets your triceps through a extension motion. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '41151201', '41151201-Cable-Overhead-Tricep-Extension-Straight-Bar-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Overhead Triceps Extension Straight Bar. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension Straight Bar', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('df1b86f1-0c42-4c17-86b2-33a8f05637b3', 'Deadlift (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Cable Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '30451201', '30451201-Cable-Deadlift-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, leg_curl, back_extension, hip_thrust, good_morning', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('df230e95-1f0b-4f49-b04a-6fe01590f76e', 'Kneeling Rear Kick (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this kicking movement focused on hip extension. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '9061201', '09061201-Band-kneeling-rear-kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Kneeling Rear Kick. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Rear Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('df2c8ebd-896d-4e91-acdb-0276eb1d6376', 'Swinging Arms Jump Split Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this lunging exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '90271201', '90271201-Swinging-Arms-Jump-Split-Lunge-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Swinging Arms Jump Split Lunge', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df2ddab1-effa-4e7f-aeb9-1927d31054df', 'Standing Diagonal Reach And Chest Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Standing Diagonal Reach And Chest Lift, an effective movement movement for upper body strength. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '70531201', '70531201-Standing-Diagonal-Reach-and-Chest-Lift-(female)_Ch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Diagonal Reach And Chest Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Standing Diagonal Reach And Chest Lift', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df42fbd3-51de-4000-9ec4-4f689c025280', 'Step Out Twist Hand Swipes', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '73531201', '73531201-Step-out-Twist-Hand-Swipes-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Step Out Twist Hand Swipes. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Out Twist Hand Swipes', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df47303e-283f-473c-814f-1e2f783f9290', 'Side Step Lateral Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Lateral Raise is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic raising movements. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '57961201', '57961201-Side-Step-Lateral-Raise-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Side Step Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df552930-3128-4956-9c55-00939ba8aeb5', 'Clamshell Sit (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Clamshell Sit Against Wall is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. The hip abductors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '89641201', '89641201-Clamshell-Sit-agains-Wall-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Clamshell Sit Against Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Clamshell Sit Against Wall', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df57f603-b39a-422d-98ea-49bc943e7e64', 'Hollow Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '12461201', '12461201-Hollow-Hold_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hollow Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hollow_hold', 'Hollow Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df66aacc-7425-43d7-a478-bc47e065e21b', 'Full Squat with Overhead Press', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '47031201', '47031201-Bodyweight-Full-Squat-with-Overhead-Press-(VERSION.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 2. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 3. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Full Squat With Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df6730ae-f44f-4929-b414-5f32bbf2ae7b', 'Kneeling Lat Pulldown (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Band Knelling Lat Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '43581201', '43581201-Band-Knelling-Lat-Pulldown_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Knelling Lat Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Knelling Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('df742795-e519-4629-90c5-b301d2442690', 'Incline Alternative Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '93081201', '93081201-Cable-Incline-Alternative-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Alternative Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Alternative Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('df86c25e-86d2-4d18-b30f-1e1ac4b0a4ba', 'Single Leg Bridge Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your glutes, chest, shoulders working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '80141201', '80141201-Single-Leg-Bridge-Pose-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 45, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Single Leg Bridge Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('df965a3c-1da9-4971-bd73-b86f9405fd3d', 'Box Drop To Single Leg Land', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '90691201', '90691201-Box-Drop-to-Single-Leg-Land-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'box_jump', 'Box Drop To Single Leg Land', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('df99a85a-31a2-4f09-b745-8fc5b6ca4b18', 'Decline Pullover (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pulling movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your lats, triceps working to support the movement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '12551201', '12551201-Barbell-Decline-Pullover_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Decline Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Pullover', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying (Decline)', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Decline Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('dfa5a1dc-e816-435b-9c34-5480ce352ef0', 'Cobra Pose With Wide Legs', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cobra Pose With Wide Legs provides a deep stretch for your abs, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79531201', '79531201-Cobra-Pose-with-Wide-Legs-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cobra Pose With Wide Legs. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cobra Pose With Wide Legs', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dfbb4e75-1b40-4e1b-9a8a-b4e3ddad602e', 'Garland Pose Sky Reach Hands Hold', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Garland Pose Sky Reach Hands Hold provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '81601201', '81601201-Garland-Pose-Sky-Reach-Hands-Hold-(female)_Stretch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Garland Pose Sky Reach Hands Hold. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Garland Pose Sky Reach Hands Hold', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dfde0782-4c72-44ee-a33a-3c363a51695f', 'Knee Cross Over (Against Wall) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Alternate Knee Cross Over Sit Against Wall is a movement exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '87671201', '87671201-Alternate-Knee-Cross-Over-Sit-agains-Wall-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, 'Static', 'Compound', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated (Against Wall)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Knee Cross Over Against Wall - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dfe1728c-d222-4d1f-beea-a8fc0347648b', 'Kneeling Fist Circle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Kneeling Fist Circle helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82471201', '82471201-Kneeling-Fist-Circle-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Fist Circle. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Kneeling Fist Circle', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dfe2a7d2-515e-43bf-b498-a923aea6d380', 'Seated Chin Tuck', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your neck with this movement exercise for improved stability. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '55011201', '55011201-Seated-Chin-Tuck-(VERSION-2)_Neck_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Chin Tuck. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your neck. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Chin Tuck', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dfe491de-4dd1-47f5-9f1a-da9750c3a3d5', 'Dancer Pose Natarajasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dancer Pose Natarajasana provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '63041201', '63041201-Dancer-Pose-Natarajasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Dancer Pose Natarajasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Dancer Pose Natarajasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dff2100c-6d27-4f4c-9cac-2990f12df68c', 'Lateral Raise (Bent Arms)', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your lateral delts with the Lateral Raise (bent Arms), an effective shoulder raising exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '54531201', '54531201-Lateral-Raise-(Bent-Arms)-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('dff5b652-b928-470d-8cdd-a4a85380b1fa', 'Seated Body Mobilization (Stability Ball)', 'Full Body', 'Stability Ball', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Seated Body Mobilization On Exercise Ball helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '98271201', '98271201-Sitting-Body-Mobilization-on-Exercise-Ball-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Seated Body Mobilization On Exercise Ball. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Body Mobilization On Exercise Ball. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 30, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'mobility', 'Seated Body Mobilization On Exercise Ball', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'stability_ball', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e000a696-e734-4e9b-b56e-5e601f7edf63', 'Standing Single Delt Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '97281201', '97281201-Cable-Standing-Single-Delt-Row-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Single Delt Row. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Single Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e0011171-7ef2-4dae-8b7d-f6ba571ed26e', 'Lying Crossover Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Crossover Stretch (side Pov) is a lower body stretching exercise that targets your chest. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '6151201', '06151201-Lying-Crossover-Stretch-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Crossover Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lying Crossover Stretch', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0035600-facb-427f-9fb1-74899ba8c22b', 'Handstand Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Handstand Push Up is an arm pushing exercise targeting your chest. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '23831201', '23831201-Handstand-Push-Up-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. An effective movement for your arms routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Handstand Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e00d8679-7a66-478f-8f36-64bc0781a630', 'Single Leg Squat With Support', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '23751201', '23751201-Single-Leg-Squat-with-Support-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat With Support', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e016023a-7361-41c2-8ebe-5a09b4e51180', 'Front Raise - Vertical Grip (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Dumbbell Standing Alternate Vertical Front Raises, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '12301201', '12301201-Dumbbell-Standing-Alternate-Vertical-Front-Raises_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Alternate Vertical Front Raises. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Standing Vertical Front Raise - Alternating', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e02ad31d-a26c-4600-bc0b-4b397c9f174d', 'Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74171201', '74171201-Overhead-Sit-up-with-Legs-on-Bench-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0319be7-b651-4638-a140-19e6b87d4ea6', 'Stepjack Front Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity raising exercise that challenges your entire body. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '56391201', '56391201-Stepjack-Front-Raise-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Stepjack Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e035b1f3-810f-4752-b553-3caff1b574a5', 'Lying Rear Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your rear delts. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '3481201', '03481201-Dumbbell-Lying-Rear-Lateral-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e038c36a-0129-447e-8a8b-30035ff1c76f', 'Wrist Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Barbell Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '30331201', '30331201-Barbell-Wrist-Curl-(female)_Forearms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Wrist Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e03dbc35-ee2a-4151-bcd0-61df4db0f44b', 'Crescent Moon Pose Anjaneyasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '9471201', '09471201-Crescent-Moon-Pose-Anjaneyasana-(female)_Stretchin.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Crescent Moon Pose Anjaneyasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Crescent Moon Pose Anjaneyasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e043b2b5-2b29-4ae7-b6c5-836c66ab0c9b', 'Standing Backhand (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '69551201', '69551201-Cable-Standing-Backhand-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Backhand. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Backhand', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e0540c4e-8e45-4593-886f-334cf2dd01c7', 'Hanging Leg Raise (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Cable Hanging Leg Raise, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '28871201', '28871201-Cable-Hanging-Leg-Raise_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Hanging Leg Raise. 2. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Hanging Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e05e20a2-616c-44a6-9f98-8aa8bcdd4e90', 'Bicycle Crunch (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '75041201', '75041201-Suspender-Bicycle-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Bicycle Crunch. 2. Bring one knee toward chest while extending the other leg. 3. Rotate to bring opposite elbow toward the bent knee. 4. Alternate sides in a pedaling motion. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Suspender Bicycle Crunch', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e087070a-76de-46ab-94f5-e6b4e9b1e351', 'Hyperextension (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. You''ll also feel your hamstrings, lower back working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '87211201', '87211201-Dumbbell-Hyperextension-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hyperextension. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e094be2c-b1aa-42f2-9c2a-118f166fa1ef', 'Shrug (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '24801201', '24801201-Barbell-Shrug-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Pull', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand', 'Standard', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e0a401cd-f687-473e-972f-faae18ac7cb7', 'Inchworm', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '46501201', '46501201-Inchworm-(VERSION-3)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Inchworm. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'inchworm', 'Inchworm', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0b8cb3d-297e-4e0e-a327-0627c9e03392', 'Lying Spiderman Crawl', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '73351201', '73351201-Lying-Spiderman-Crawl-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Spiderman Crawl. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Spiderman Crawl. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Spiderman Crawl', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0cc2585-46bd-4be7-be9b-5e0626d9a852', '45 Degree Hyperextension Arms Crossed (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '58131201', '58131201-45-degree-Hyperextension-(arms-in-front-of-chest)-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Hip Hinge / Trunk Extension', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degree Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0df3c21-b926-4ee6-a0d8-f8bcdb9f7b5f', 'Twisting Knee Thrust', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Twisting Knee Thrust builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '51761201', '51761201-Twisting-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Ideal for full body strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Twisting Knee Thrust', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0ebea37-b48c-4d30-8450-ce68b66db0bd', 'Incline Triceps Extension (Plate)', 'Arms', 'Weight Plate', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '83241201', '83241201-Weighted-Plate-Incline-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 2. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Weighted Plate Incline Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e0f1b3a4-444a-4bc7-b636-95db34f2770a', 'Standing Forward Bent Twist - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '103561201', '103561201-Standing-Forward-Bent-Alternating-Twist-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Forward Bent Alternating Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Forward Bent Twist - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1008108-4efa-4339-b3bb-255b83eadbf9', 'Jumping Jack Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity jumping exercise that challenges your entire body. The shoulders, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75681201', '75681201-Jumping-Jack-Punch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jumping Jack Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Jumping Jack Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e10d7cae-4a59-4377-954d-7b7d3809944f', 'Side Step Folded Arms Lift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '99051201', '99051201-Side-Step-Folded-Arms-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Folded Arms Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Side Step Folded Arms Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1188952-d3e3-4bf8-ba5d-13ef2ab61055', 'Lying Leg Tuck Hip Twist Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hips, the Lying Leg Tuck Hip Twist Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '34761201', '34761201-Lying-Leg-Tuck-Hip-Twist-Stretch-(male)_Stretching.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Tuck Hip Twist Stretch. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Leg Tuck Hip Twist Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying Leg Tuck Hip Twist Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e11ad22b-ab20-432c-b53f-b3d730b1125a', 'Good Morning (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this movement exercise. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '441201', '00441201-Barbell-Good-Morning_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Good Morning. 2. Set up in the starting position for Barbell Good Morning. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Hip Hinge', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated), On Bar', 'Standard', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e130db88-6547-471d-9045-45bf5a600d44', 'T Bar Delt Row - Wide Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever T Bar Wide Grip Delt Row is a rowing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '104231201', '104231201-Lever-T-Bar-Wide-Grip-Delt-Row_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever T Bar Wide Grip Delt Row. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 't_bar_row', 'Lever T Bar Delt Row - Wide Grip', 'Lever T Bar Delt Row - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e1353a21-9817-4e06-bb84-8a1c08a68d75', 'Seated Shoulder Tap (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Shoulder Tap On A Chair is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '86521201', '86521201-Seated-Shoulder-Tap-on-a-Chair-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. An effective movement for your arms routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulder Tap On A Chair', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e13c2e21-aeea-4bc3-9d97-55de2d425199', 'Lying Knee Flexion (Machine)', 'Core', 'Lever Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this flexion movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '96761201', '96761201-Lever-Lying-Knee-Flexion-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lying Knee Flexion. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lever Lying Knee Flexion. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lever Lying Knee Flexion', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e142258b-ee91-4866-9930-e348d2e6ad17', 'Standing Palms In Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '25991201', '25991201-Dumbbell-Standing-Palms-In-Press-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Palms In Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Palms In Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e14a6480-95d2-44cf-a9e3-ca2935c2b52e', 'Side Plank With Raised Leg', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Side Plank With Raised Leg, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '49071201', '49071201-Side-Plank-with-Raised-Leg-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Beneficial for overall core development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank With Raised Leg', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e16030fd-6376-4271-950c-dd2861b47458', 'Standing Hammer Curl To Press (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Hammer Curl To Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '73601201', '73601201-Dumbbell-Standing-Hammer-Curl-to-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Hammer Curl To Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 4. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 5. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 6. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Standing Hammer Curl To Press', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e1655a10-647b-4c72-8768-bf059da71894', 'Lying Hip Internal Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your hips with this rotation stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '81511201', '81511201-Lying-Hip-Internal-Rotation-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Internal Rotation. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Hip Internal Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Lying Hip Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e167b96c-1c12-4c87-891c-584300f09634', 'Decline Pullover - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your lats, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '371201', '00371201-Barbell-Decline-Wide-Grip-Pullover_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Decline Wide Grip Pullover. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 4. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Pullover', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Decline Pullover - Wide Grip', 'Decline Pullover - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e1686cc8-8960-45fe-bdf0-3846e56c2466', 'Otis Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Otis Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '38371201', '38371201-Otis-Up-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Otis Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Otis Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e16aaf52-7f45-44e0-814c-1ea5d0fa8f50', 'Hollow Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '71571201', '71571201-Hollow-Hold-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hollow Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hollow_hold', 'Hollow Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1720536-da96-4d30-8977-bcba138551d4', 'Back Toe Tap Walk - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '97781201', '97781201-Alternating-Back-Toe-Tap-Walk-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternating Back Toe Tap Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Back Toe Tap Walk - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e17f279c-5d35-449e-81fb-f9068bd6c4e5', 'Body Saw Plank', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this stabilization movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '43841201', '43841201-Body-Saw-Plank_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. This variation specifically emphasizes the delts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Body Saw Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1840a18-e04a-45de-ad2b-dd26d8b174e4', 'Lying Single Leg Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '93061201', '93061201-Resistance-Band-Lying-Single-Leg-Curl-(female)_Thi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Lying Single Leg Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Resistance Band Lying Single Leg Curl. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lying Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e18a4144-e980-449b-a987-a6c24898a1bf', 'Behind The Head Clap', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this movement movement. You''ll also feel your rear delts working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '64491201', '64491201-Behind-The-Head-Clap-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Behind The Head Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Behind The Head Clap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e191bbdf-fc45-44ad-9087-eeea262fbd19', 'Side Shuffle Swing', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side Shuffle Swing builds reactive power and improves conditioning. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '75701201', '75701201-Side-Shuffle-Swing-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Side Shuffle Swing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e19a9e16-1c58-4bb8-845a-31f93f64085e', 'Hip Extension Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Hip Extension Stretch is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '46731201', '46731201-Hip-Extension-Stretch-(male)_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Hip Extension Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hip Extension Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Hip Extension Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1a3beba-64c8-4471-9099-908d5dd69938', 'Single Leg Deadlift', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '81031201', '81031201-Bodyweight-Single-Leg-Deadlift-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 2. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 3. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Single Leg Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1b55d27-0f34-4c5b-a16a-61bb3fcf73ba', 'Curtsey Lunge Hand Swipes', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this lunging exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '68891201', '68891201-Curtsey-Lunge-Hand-Swipes-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. A solid choice for plyometrics day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Curtsey Lunge Hand Swipes', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1bfa371-0497-4454-ba83-b8e7c39a7f06', 'Downward Dog Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Downward Dog Squat provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your hamstrings, shoulders working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '89671201', '89671201-Downward-Dog-Squat-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog Squat', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1c3f8f0-d31e-4e37-9f0f-8f42ba540bb9', 'Single Stiff Leg Deadlift With Single Arm Row (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Band Single Stiff Leg Deadlift With Single Arm Row targets your hamstrings through a controlled rowing motion. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '37731201', '37731201-Band-Single-Stiff-Leg-Deadlift-with-Single-Arm-Row.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Single Stiff Leg Deadlift With Single Arm Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Single Stiff Leg Deadlift With Single Arm Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e1cf7f64-3519-4061-9698-7482ffbe55f3', 'Lateral to Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lateral To Front Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '74031201', '74031201-Dumbbell-Lateral-to-Front-Raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lateral To Front Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Lateral To Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e1d2020f-80cb-4c5b-b4fb-a154fdef51a6', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '46671201', '46671201-Bodyweight-Overhead-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 2. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1d78430-28fe-46fc-915a-bd73b2e57ea7', 'Leg Raise Hold (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '66331201', '66331201-Leg-Raises-Hold-on-Chair-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Leg Raise Hold On Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1e397e7-fad9-4274-824d-408672e4c3c2', 'Side Lying Scissors', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '46551201', '46551201-Side-Lying-Scissors_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Scissors. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Lying Scissors', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1ea9177-9043-498a-8e29-d1db96663c83', 'Single Arm Military Press To The Side (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '5391201', '05391201-Kettlebell-One-Arm-Military-Press-To-The-Side_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell One Arm Military Press To The Side. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Single Arm Military Press To The Side', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('e1fa6215-cd50-4d1c-94d7-667535534cbb', 'Cross Left Uppercut Cross Left Hook (combo)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '104441201', '104441201-Cross-Left-Uppercut-Cross-Left-Hook-(combo)_Boxing.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cross Left Uppercut Cross Left Hook. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Cross Left Uppercut Cross Left Hook', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1fb3a42-f84a-4477-a0b0-aa5dba91a914', 'Bicep Curl - Side Lying', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '17691201', '17691201-Bodyweight-Side-Lying-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Side Lying Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e1ff9aa4-59b8-4bee-940c-e0dba951c9a7', 'Seated Butterfly Knee Raise - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '81521201', '81521201-Seated-Alternate-Butterfly-Knee-Raise-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Butterfly Knee Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e21ad1a3-67d7-4210-9da6-2a069767e538', 'Elbow Touch And Press Up', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '76341201', '76341201-Elbow-Touch-and-Press-Up-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 2. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 3. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Elbow Touch And Press Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e22b5125-5160-44ae-8d0f-6cb5816d818f', 'Ring Hip Lift Single Leg Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Ring Hip Lift Single Leg Curl targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '65861201', '65861201-Ring-Hip-Lift-Single-Leg-Curl-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Ring Hip Lift Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e24f6929-12f2-4048-8e66-0037f3ad9260', 'Cat Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Cat Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '9421201', '09421201-Cat-pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cat Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Cat Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2602bd2-9a32-455b-92fc-b1d577fc6315', 'Hammer Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Hammer Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '91341201', '91341201-Resistance-Band-Hammer-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Hammer Curl', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e2640054-29de-4afb-b95a-fd851c9ea06c', 'Weighted Lying Side Lifting Head (With Head Harness)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Weighted Lying Side Lifting Head (with Head Harnes, focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '8381201', '08381201-Weighted-Lying-Side-Lifting-Head-(with-head-harnes.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Lying Side Lifting Head (with Head Harnes. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Weighted Lying Side Lifting Head (with Head Harnes', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e27b865c-fd73-45d6-b8c6-cd61cdeb946d', 'Hammer Strict Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '59201201', '59201201-Dumbbell-Hammer-Srtict-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hammer Strict Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Hammer Strict Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e27bb9b6-3b52-4168-97a0-0826e62af7a3', 'Hip Thrust (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this thrusting movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '47421201', '47421201-Dumbbell-Hip-Thrust_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hip Thrust. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e28254da-076e-4b35-99ab-f1b5c1583174', 'Single Arm Leg Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Suspender One Arm Leg Push Up, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '11251201', '11251201-Suspender-One-Arm-Leg-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender One Arm Leg Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Single Arm Leg Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e283decd-d411-4dad-9f0f-7f7015ca2cb4', 'Heels Squat Slide (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '87641201', '87641201-Heels-Squat-Slide-Wall-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Heels Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2850dd5-a745-4cb9-93c9-40aa52dfe4b8', 'Squat (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11431201', '11431201-Suspender-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Suspender Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e29c0876-2f70-4272-b791-1a79bac75263', 'Incline Fly (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Band Incline Fly is a flying exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '68471201', '68471201-Band-Incline-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e29c375b-dfd6-4d86-b7d8-0f08dc2f27df', 'Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this kicking movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '80831201', '80831201-Cable-Straight-Leg-Diagonal-Kickback-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Great for building strength in your glutes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Diagonal Kickback', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e2a46362-1465-4f0c-96c5-f947ca5e1e40', 'Plank Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '89501201', '89501201-Plank-Row-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Row', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2abf1f0-4dd7-4292-a2da-461cab62cb84', 'Side Step Arm Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Arm Curl is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic curling movements. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '62061201', '62061201-Side-Step-Arm-Curl-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Side Step Arm Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2b63a79-5104-45f6-8462-c74cb2e31529', 'Superman Open Up', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Superman Open Up is a lower body movement exercise that targets your lower back. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '96261201', '96261201-Superman-Open-Up-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Superman Open Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Superman Open Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2b7e878-d271-455e-b2e1-c0b93ce4141a', 'Chair Sit Heel Raise (Against Wall) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Wall, Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '87381201', '87381201-Chair-Sit-Alternate-Heel-Raise-agains-Wall-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Chair Sit Alternate Heel Raise Against Wall. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Chair Sit Heel Raise Against Wall - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2bc1933-6578-4801-be5c-22a20e3bd1a6', 'Seated Cross Body Punch (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '84241201', '84241201-Seated-Cross-Body-Punch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Seated Cross Body Punch On A Chair', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2c12dfc-fe3c-4207-8eba-10b483b0c9b8', 'Standing Swim And Jog', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Swim And Jog builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '89271201', '89271201-Standing-Swim-and-Jog-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Swim And Jog. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'swimming', 'Standing Swim And Jog', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2ca8ab4-8ae3-42a8-a867-2bbf5c936ad1', 'Plank Prone Plate Switch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '65981201', '65981201-Plank-Prone-Plate-Switch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Plank Prone Plate Switch. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Prone Plate Switch', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2cee968-b091-498b-9674-0793a821f7a5', 'Kneeling Hip Opener Into Forward Lunge And Hamstri', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '83871201', '83871201-Kneeling-Hip-Opener-into-Forward-Lunge-and-Hamstri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Kneeling Hip Opener Into Forward Lunge And Hamstri', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2db9ad6-977c-446a-a47b-f75789619925', 'Assisted Pull Up (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '38441201', '38441201-Band-Assisted-Pull-Up-(VERSION-3)-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Assisted Pull Up. 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Assisted Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e2eb5554-8d2f-4b26-9d7c-0c6bee7a5f3e', 'Standing Balance Fist Up Side Leg Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your hip abductors. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '85811201', '85811201-Standing-Balance-Fist-Up-Side-Leg-Raise-(male)_Ply.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Balance Fist Up Side Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2f2713a-f815-48c1-a244-9126d17cd2d0', 'Standing Hip Controlled Articular Rotation', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Standing Hip Controlled Articular Rotation is a compound rotation exercise that engages your entire body. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '67131201', '67131201-Standing-Hip-Controlled-Articular-Rotation-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Hip Controlled Articular Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mobility', 'Standing Hip Controlled Articular Rotation', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e2fef018-1a89-442a-8935-b0a1b4807a9b', 'Weighted Sissy Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '40321201', '40321201-Weighted-Sissy-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. An effective movement for your legs routine. Variation: Weighted Sissy Squat.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Weighted Sissy Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e30bb44c-939d-4624-a985-877e5dea85ec', 'Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '22201201', '22201201-Dumbbell-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e3127c6f-c403-4f5f-8960-71ae74815419', 'Vibrate Plate Lunge (Vibration Plate)', 'Legs', 'Vibration Plate', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Vibrate Plate Lunge provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '25271201', '25271201-Vibrate-Plate-Lunge-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Vibrate Plate Lunge. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Vibrate Plate Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e35689d1-0564-4515-a435-8fe24c170d5d', 'Sled 45 Calf Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Sled 45 Calf Press isolates your calf muscles through a pressing motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '7381201', '07381201-Sled-45-Calf-Press_Calves-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Execute the pressing motion for Sled 45 Calf Press, extending through the target muscles. 2. Set up in the starting position for Sled 45 Calf Press. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Sled 45 Calf Press', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e35fd0c4-4108-4e66-beb5-c0ac89a3477c', 'Frog Pump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Frog Pump is a hip-dominant movement exercise that targets your glutes. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '31811201', '31811201-Bodyweight-Frog-Pump-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Frog Pump. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Frog Pump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e36aeb96-f67c-41cd-b55f-7fa8cc452e58', 'Slight Squat Torso Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Slight Squat Torso Twist. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '85801201', '85801201-Slight-Squat-Torso-Twist-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. Great for building strength in your obliques.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Slight Squat Torso Twist', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e36dc3ed-4d0e-42d8-b8c7-96c1d2ea98f9', 'Cat Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '2491201', '02491201-Cat-Stretch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cat Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Cat Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e37757ea-b8eb-45bb-ad28-a068b5525ba1', 'Side Lying Hip Adduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Side Lying Hip Adduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your adductors. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '46571201', '46571201-Side-Lying-Hip-Adduction-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Hip Adduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Side Lying Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e37b3b61-de42-422e-83bc-fc5aeda6ab59', 'Single Leg Low Box Squat (Plyo Box)', 'Legs', 'Plyo Box', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '70311201', '70311201-Single-Leg-Low-Box-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Single Leg Low Box Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e37e517e-cbb8-44ce-8200-2c4b8d3bc9d9', 'Double Elbow Raise And Double Elbow Clap', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '94171201', '94171201-Double-Elbow-Raise-and-Double-Elbow-Clap-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Double Elbow Raise And Double Elbow Clap. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Double Elbow Raise And Double Elbow Clap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e38e8f4d-febc-4ca8-a411-865c19ff4bbd', 'Reverse Lunge Knee Drive', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '73361201', '73361201-Reverse-Lunge-Knee-Drive-(front-POV)-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Reverse Lunge Knee Drive', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e39f9d56-458d-4b28-947c-7357b0ebf6d1', 'Isometric Wipers', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Isometric Wipers is a movement exercise that targets your chest muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '5001201', '05001201-Isometric-Wipers_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Isometric Wipers. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Isometric Wipers', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e3a96e04-6e1a-4d31-8859-1674a560eb3e', 'Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '2891201', '02891201-Dumbbell-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e3c0106b-8eea-41c2-acfd-f220239adb54', 'Pigeon Pose Rock To Active Quad Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your hips with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '79181201', '79181201-Pigeon-Pose-Rock-to-Active-Quad-Stretch-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Pigeon Pose Rock To Active Quad Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'quad_stretch', 'Pigeon Pose Rock To Active Quad Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('e3c5f91d-9f0d-4f1b-9a0c-8df271e1461e', 'Hip Flexor Stretch Rear Foot Elevated (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your hip flexors area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '46741201', '46741201-Hip-Flexor-Stretch-Rear-foot-elevated-(male)_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Hip Flexor Stretch Rear Foot Elevated. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Hip Flexor Stretch Rear Foot Elevated', 'split_squat, lunge, leg_press', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e3c611e8-82b7-4024-be51-bfbda5a3b25d', 'Lying Hip Lift (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '10651201', '10651201-Lying-Hip-Lift-(on-stability-ball)-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Lying Hip Lift. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Lift. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Hip Lift', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e3cd6779-e24d-42e0-8aa4-b8b89c549cdb', 'Incline Press - Reverse Grip (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Chest","Triceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Barbell Incline Reverse Grip Press strengthens your forearms and grip through a pressing motion. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '481201', '00481201-Barbell-Incline-Reverse-Grip-Press_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Reverse Grip Press. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Execute the pressing motion for Barbell Incline Reverse Grip Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Incline Press - Reverse Grip', 'Incline Press - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e3d01780-aba1-4abc-b9fb-11697c35ef38', 'Bird Dog Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your lower back, the Bird Dog Hold helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your glutes, abs working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78021201', '78021201-Bird-Dog-Hold-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Bird Dog Hold. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Bird Dog Hold', 'dead_bug, plank, back_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e3d1129f-647c-4105-a24a-7395ccacbf69', 'Toe Raise (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '13961201', '13961201-Smith-Toe-Raise_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Toe Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Smith Toe Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Smith Toe Raise', 'Toe Raise', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e3d5861b-390c-4c27-bd52-0ca368b75030', 'Lunge (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Band Lunges is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '9091201', '09091201-Band-Lunges-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Lunges. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e3df1164-9747-4408-8cc8-e20274cda4d3', 'Walking On Stepmill', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walking On Stepmill is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '24901201', '24901201-Walking-on-Stepmill-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Stepmill. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Stepmill', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e3e25c32-fd47-4046-99e3-7ed89411e453', 'Standing Curl Straight Bar - Reverse Grip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '29531201', '29531201-Cable-Standing-Reverse-Grip-Curl-(Straight-bar)-(female)_Forearms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Reverse Grip Curl. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Curl - Reverse Grip', 'Standing Curl - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e3fc865c-a76e-4af4-86ad-de15c86e1326', 'Rotating Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your neck area and enhance overall flexibility. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '81871201', '81871201-Rotating-Neck-Stretch-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Rotating Neck Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 32, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Rotating Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e401ac9a-8010-46a8-a482-1f0c2a380f24', 'Deadlift Back', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Deadlift Back targets your hamstrings through a controlled hip hinge motion. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '23541201', '23541201-Deadlift---Back-(WRONG-RIGHT)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 2. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 3. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift Back', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4155a08-72f0-4230-9bb4-94e6841c575a', 'Seated Bench Face Pull (Rope)', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Cable Seated Bench Face Pull (with Rope) is a flexibility exercise that targets your rear delts, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The upper back, rotator cuff assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '98251201', '98251201-Cable-Sitting-Bench-Face-Pull-(with-rope)-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Bench Face Pull. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Seated Bench Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e419c4ff-6077-429d-89cc-6f4296876215', 'Yin Yang Leg Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Yin Yang Leg Lift is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '68601201', '68601201-Yin-Yang-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Yin Yang Leg Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Yin Yang Leg Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e42ec938-1ebb-47b2-a580-e3c2187274aa', 'Front Rack Split Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '65561201', '65561201-Barbell-Front-Rack-Split Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Front Rack Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Front Rack Split Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e43df8c0-c97d-49fc-be41-be1938e8c71d', 'Side Bend (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Cable Side Bend is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '25761201', '25761201-Cable-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Side Bend. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e44a8b8b-09c5-4692-84f0-ea5dcd6b3277', 'Side Step Top And Forward Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '72721201', '72721201-Side-Step-Top-and-Forward-Punch-(female)_Plyometri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Top And Forward Punch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Side Step Top And Forward Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e44c41d0-aa76-413c-b215-fb1ea8600416', '90 Degrees Internal Rotation Catch (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this rotation movement that develops pressing power. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '105971201', '105971201-Cable-90-degrees-Internal-Rotation-Catch-(male)_C.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable 90 Degrees Internal Rotation Catch. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable 90 Degrees Internal Rotation Catch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', '90 Degrees Internal Rotation Catch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e45dfe25-04e1-4750-b084-dc3db7f8502c', 'Chin Tuck (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Chin Tuck Against The Wall targets your neck muscles through a controlled movement motion. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '95361201', '95361201-Chin-Tuck-against-the-Wall-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Chin Tuck Against The Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your neck. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Chin Tuck Against The Wall', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e467eb0e-3487-47f2-9361-0f763520f20f', 'Seated Rear Delt Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Cable Seated Rear Delt Raise is a raising exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '70601201', '70601201-Cable-Seated-Rear-Delt-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Rear Delt Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides and back, focusing on rear delts. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Seated Rear Delt Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, face_pull, bent_over_row', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e46f8ecb-09f1-4140-b4d4-42faa6126f46', 'Lying Leg Raise And Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Leg Raise And Hold is a lower body raising exercise that targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '71181201', '71181201-Lying-Leg-Raise-and-Hold-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Raise And Hold. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Leg Raise And Hold', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e473eab9-701a-40f2-9feb-51c19b571f97', 'Decline Overhead Sit Up (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '47341201', '47341201-Dumbbell-Decline-Overhead-Sit-up_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Overhead Sit Up. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Decline Overhead Sit Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Sit Up', NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Decline Overhead Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e4744a31-9205-469a-b80f-9fc69f5b2be3', 'Standing Row (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Standing Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91451201', '91451201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Row. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e4782bd8-e03a-47c4-a517-8fbd19aedc87', 'Cross Body Heel Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'The Cross Body Heel Tap is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '80351201', '80351201-Cross-Body-Heel-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cross Body Heel Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Cross Body Heel Tap', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e47f2b32-1903-4a34-bd53-b2ff9e21098e', 'Hanging Tucked Front Hold (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Hanging Tucked Front Lever Hold is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your hip flexors, grip work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '90431201', '90431201-Hanging-Tucked-Front-Lever-Hold-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Hanging Tucked Front Lever Hold. 2. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 3. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_lever', 'Hanging Tucked Front Lever Hold', 'pull_up, lat_pulldown, grip_training', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e48bb856-02a5-4a93-b7de-2984c1a2581c', 'Half Kneeling Chop (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this movement exercise that strengthens your obliques. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '45731201', '45731201-Band-Half-Kneeling-Chop_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Half Kneeling Chop. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 55, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Half Kneeling Chop', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e48ddf36-f38c-4ab9-8267-6ad8e7609d36', 'Middle Fly (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '9131201', '09131201-Band-Middle-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Middle Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Middle Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e48f346b-cf1f-4eec-87db-2810d24fec06', 'Angled Single Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '93871201', '93871201-Lever-Angled-Single-Leg-Press-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Angled Single Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Angled Single Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e49fe232-1de1-484f-bdce-91b05238a161', 'Seated Lateral Raise (Resistance Band, Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Chair', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '91411201', '91411201-Resistance-Band-Sitting-Lateral-Raise-on-a-Chair-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Lateral Raise On A Chair. 2. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 5. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Lateral Raise On A Chair', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e4a2f672-c369-4112-ad5f-53a179c32603', 'Rear Delt Row (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rowing movement focusing on your rear delts. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '10061201', '10061201-Band-Rear-Delt-Row_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Rear Delt Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e4ad1f25-fd3d-4d27-8ff5-9232b88451e0', 'Reverse Hyperextension (Stability Ball)', 'Back', 'Stability Ball, Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this extension movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '90091201', '90091201-Reverse-Hyperextension-on-Stability-Ball-(male)_Hi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Reverse Hyperextension On Stability Ball. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Reverse Hyperextension On Stability Ball', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4b18827-1275-4231-9755-2e2dff7fdc81', 'Calves Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted stretching exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '45101201', '45101201-Calves-stretch-(male)_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Calves Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Calves Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4bb63f3-d5c6-4f5c-b941-2fe38a32f78f', 'Standing Side Bend (Bent Arm)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '32551201', '32551201-Standing-Side-Bend-(bent-arm)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4bd9da0-70a4-41d4-afb1-7c99988e4218', 'Standing Inverted Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '92061201', '92061201-Standing-Inverted-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Inverted Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4c44b54-7342-469b-a682-6d3e12991e8c', 'Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Kettlebell Swing, a comprehensive swinging exercise. You''ll also feel your glutes, core working to support the movement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '25371201', '25371201-Kettlebell-Swing-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Swing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('e4e06d32-0ffe-4df1-a40a-8edc4c73b9b8', 'Staggered Leg Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '74181201', '74181201-Staggered-Leg-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Perfect for targeting your glutes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Staggered Leg Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e4eb8742-c5a6-4276-8a7f-c7ceaf3cc55b', 'Hamstrings Lying Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Hamstrings Lying Stretch targets your hamstrings through a controlled stretching motion. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '14061201', '14061201-Hamstrings-Lying-Stretch-(female)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Hamstrings Lying Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hamstrings Lying Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Hamstrings Lying Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e503714a-fe4b-4820-9004-8b835cec0295', 'Seated Single Leg Curl (Plate Loaded)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Single Leg Curl (plate Loaded) targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Secondary activation of your calves provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '107631201', '107631201-Lever-Seated-Single-Leg-Curl-(plate-loaded)-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Leg Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Seated Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e5095e41-4035-4482-a682-29be9b864053', 'Thomas Frontal Test', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Thomas Frontal Test is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '67951201', '67951201-Thomas-Frontal-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Thomas Frontal Test. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Thomas Frontal Test', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e50e2885-f37d-41d8-8f7a-87f315d40728', 'Banded Hip Thrust (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this thrusting movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '104181201', '104181201-Barbell-Banded-Hip-Thrust_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Banded Hip Thrust. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Banded Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e5124f94-0d3d-4161-bf9e-eaab737ac696', 'Seated Lean Back (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lean Back On A Chair is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '84231201', '84231201-Seated-Lean-Back-on-a-Chair-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Lean Back On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5164506-c926-4687-a2d5-8b18aae415e1', 'Seated Lateral Raise (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lateral Raise On A Chair is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '90981201', '90981201-Sitting-Lateral-Raise-on-a-Chair-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Lateral Raise On A Chair', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e51b9fc1-9f6f-4ed9-b548-7790089f9647', 'Seated Swimmer (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Seated Swimmer On A Chair builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '91601201', '91601201-Sitting-Swimmer-on-a-Chair-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'swimming', 'Seated Swimmer On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e51c39b6-643c-40d4-ab49-847f7e492712', 'Standing Prone Y Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Prone Y Raise is a raising exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '83341201', '83341201-Dumbbell-Standing-Prone-Y-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Prone Y Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Standing Prone Y Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Prone Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e528869c-24b3-4d17-afb0-fb720adc020a', 'Side Step Diagonal Reaches', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side Step Diagonal Reaches builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '79491201', '79491201-Side-Step-Diagonal-Reaches-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Diagonal Reaches. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Step Diagonal Reaches', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e529309a-1055-4dcf-86b0-0b78d4743d4a', 'Bent Leg Kickback (kneeling)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this kicking movement focused on hip extension. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '14741201', '14741201-Bent-Leg-Kickback-(kneeling)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Bent Leg Kickback', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e539ad25-c4de-4a28-9774-257ef9bac357', 'Pullover (Plate)', 'Chest', 'Weight Plate', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Weighted Plate Pullover is a pulling exercise that develops back strength and muscle. You''ll also feel your lats, triceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '83221201', '83221201-Weighted-Plate-Pullover-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 2. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Weighted Plate Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5421fd6-c598-4e1f-9406-5c2a2a3a0680', 'Single Arm Push Up (Against Wall)', 'Chest', 'Wall', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Wall Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '96131201', '96131201-Single-Arm-Wall-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Single Arm Wall Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e56972f4-cf6f-4240-af5a-93934ecad1b3', 'Curl (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The EZ Barbell Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '22381201', '22381201-EZ-Barbell-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'EZ Curl', 'EZ Curl', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e5720ffe-0904-4f36-9d27-9da14efe6958', 'Plyo Squat Side Bend', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Plyo Squat Side Bend is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '84071201', '84071201-Plyo-Squat-Side-Bend-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Plyo Squat Side Bend', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e57e32f4-0975-4217-ae19-74ac12e9126b', 'Clean High Pull (Barbell)', 'Full Body', 'Barbell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Glutes","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint pulling movement. You''ll also feel your quads, glutes, traps working to support the movement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '57051201', '57051201-Barbell-Clean-High-Pull_Weightlifts_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Clean High Pull. 2. Explosively pull the weight upward from the starting position. 3. Pull yourself under the weight and catch it at shoulder level. 4. Stand to complete the lift, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Clean High Pull', 'power_clean, deadlift, front_squat', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e586844d-81c4-43dc-b0a0-675ce996f57c', 'Forward Fold Squat Mobilization', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your quads area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '98181201', '98181201-Forward-Fold-Squat-Mobilization-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 73, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Forward Fold Squat Mobilization', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e591d1bc-d053-47b4-ba12-addcca9d5d73', 'Side Lying Internal Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Side Lying Internal Rotation, an effective shoulder rotation exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '72131201', '72131201-Side-Lying-Internal-Rotation-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Side Lying Internal Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Side Lying Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5978ea4-155a-451f-9d2d-0d4109b265e3', 'Middle Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '97301201', '97301201-Cable-Middle-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to mid-height (chest level) and attach the appropriate handle. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Middle Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e5a0e685-96aa-4b70-b177-9b86e93a4ec5', 'Lying Extension Pullover - Rope Attachment (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pulling movement that develops pressing power. The lats, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '1841201', '01841201-Cable-Lying-Extension-Pullover-(with-rope-attachme.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Extension Pullover (with Rope Attachme. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Extension Pullover (with Rope Attachme. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Cable Lying Extension Pullover (with Rope Attachme. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Lying Extension Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e5ac7b46-d957-45a3-8e01-4947ac2332ea', 'Reverse Spider Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '55191201', '55191201-Barbell-Reverse-Spider-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Reverse Spider Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Reverse Spider Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e5c917d8-2d76-4c01-84a2-cf84238eab6b', 'Wide Stance Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '84571201', '84571201-Wide-Stance-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wide Stance Side Bend. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Wide Stance Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5cf2136-2738-4e91-8cf0-f2f49be88c60', 'Bent Leg Side Kick (kneeling)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Bent Leg Side Kick (kneeling) is a lower body kicking exercise that targets your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '14751201', '14751201-Bent-Leg-Side-Kick-(kneeling)-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Bent Leg Side Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Bent Leg Side Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5d7c27d-d075-4b33-925a-520e4bef20a0', 'Kneeling Medial Hamstring Groin Reach (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your core, the Kneeling Medial Hamstring Groin Reach helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '83801201', '83801201-Kneeling-Medial-Hamstring-Groin-Reach-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Medial Hamstring Groin Reach. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Medial Hamstring Groin Reach', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e5dc73cf-c1fe-4506-9706-f4f0e1baae75', 'Sit Up To Mountain Hop', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '74981201', '74981201-Sit-up-to-Mountain Hop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sit Up To Mountain Hop. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Sit Up To Mountain Hop', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5e160eb-d8bd-4109-be88-33cb3fb9820c', 'Kneeling Wrist Sinkers', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Wrist Sinkers strengthens your forearms and grip through a movement motion. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '77751201', '77751201-Kneeling-Wrist-Sinkers-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Wrist Sinkers. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Wrist Sinkers', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5e7a131-e641-4af4-9608-2aa038f2849a', 'Side Walk Elbow Open', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '92561201', '92561201-Side-Walk-Elbow-Open-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Walk Elbow Open. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Side Walk Elbow Open', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e5f2e432-a326-4ab2-97f6-eaf237f85d06', 'Mountain Climber (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this climbing movement focusing on your abs. The hip flexors, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '10841201', '10841201-Suspender-Mountain-Climber-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Mountain Climber. 2. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 3. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 4. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 40, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Suspender Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e5ff3626-1da3-4047-9224-a8e192071e34', 'Pistol Squat (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lever Pistol Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '10401201', '10401201-Lever-Pistol-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Pistol Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'pistol_squat', 'Lever Pistol Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e6043390-2f27-44b0-ac9f-a75f396a4ef0', 'Full Squat (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '10391201', '10391201-Lever-Full-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Full Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Lever Full Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e6082981-1c26-47a1-b988-02989b19afc3', 'Pistol Squat (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '71331201', '71331201-Pistol-Squat-with-Chair_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Pistol Squat With Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e61410ec-aa48-4d2b-949e-d108cc8fd52b', 'Lying Leg Raise Hip (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '21571201', '21571201-Resistance-Band-Lying-Leg-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Lying Leg Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Resistance Band Lying Leg Raise. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e626e4e9-0c44-4f22-b844-fab9692d9565', 'Kneeling Lateral Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your lats area and enhance overall flexibility. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '84861201', '84861201-Kneeling-Lateral-Lunge-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Kneeling Lateral Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e627a8d7-4a33-4d7b-9080-cfe85f24d279', 'Standing Single Arm Concentration Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '4211201', '04211201-Dumbbell-Standing-One-Arm-Concentration-Curl_Upper.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 89, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Standing Single Arm Concentration Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e6282ecf-0248-4aa5-9384-adb57b36f276', 'Rear Pull Up - Wide Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '36281201', '36281201-Wide-Grip-Rear-Pull-Up-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Rear Pull Up - Wide Grip', 'Rear Pull Up - Wide Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e62c1d0d-70d3-4bac-81fc-1c5ee3333a4d', 'Single Arm Rear Delt Row (TRX)', 'Shoulders', 'TRX', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Single Arm Rear Delt Row is a rowing exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '11331201', '11331201-Suspender-Single-Arm-Rear-Delt-Row-(female)_Should.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Single Arm Rear Delt Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Suspender Single Arm Rear Delt Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e6412f7f-8919-412e-8b95-0d0a444c6309', 'Walking Low Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '97001201', '97001201-Bodyweight-Walking-Low-Lunge-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge, then bring your back foot forward for the next step. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 70, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Low Lunge', 'lunge, split_squat, step_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e652a816-8521-4114-be23-018d97ef533c', 'Side Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Side Push Up is an arm pushing exercise targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '7171201', '07171201-Side-Push-up_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Side Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e652b9a5-fd0f-45d6-9d33-7b733039f1dc', 'Lying Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '11631201', '11631201-Lying-Leg-Raise_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e657bb98-7be8-479e-a337-8a45f0030e3c', 'Standing Military Press (Smith Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Smith Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '7741201', '07741201-Smith-Standing-Military-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Standing Military Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Smith Standing Military Press', 'Standing Military Press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e665ba51-28f8-47d6-a6c6-1241ded80d83', 'Kneeling Back And Side Leg Lift', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '94521201', '94521201-Kneeling-Back-and-Side-Leg-Lift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Back And Side Leg Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Kneeling Back And Side Leg Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e668fea4-67a8-4c3e-9159-3aa6c6bebe45', 'Hang Snatch (Barbell)', 'Full Body', 'Barbell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Barbell Hang Snatch, a comprehensive movement exercise. Secondary activation of your quads, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '15221201', '15221201-Barbell-Hang-Snatch_Weightlifts-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Hang Snatch. 2. Explosively pull the weight from the floor/hang position. 3. As it rises, pull yourself under and catch it overhead with locked arms. 4. Stand to complete the lift. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'snatch', 'Hang Snatch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e66c7e70-7882-4a68-8e89-aa8a0d687830', 'Walking On Stepmill', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '23111201', '23111201-Walking-on-Stepmill_Cardio.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Stepmill. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Stepmill', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e671e055-48dd-4d77-a4bf-74b797c2b350', 'Floor Press (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '29831201', '29831201-Dumbbell-Alternating-Floor-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternating Floor Press. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Alternating Floor Press. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Floor Press - Alternating', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e68fbfb2-c2e1-4043-8a8e-731c92ede78d', 'Incline Hammer Curl (Band) - Alternating', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68711201', '68711201-Band-Incline-Alternate-Hammer-Curl_Upper-Arms1_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Alternate Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Incline Hammer Curl - Alternating', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e6bb2a9c-ee47-4295-b1ec-862e6e19271f', 'Press On Floor (Kettlebell) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '5191201', '05191201-Kettlebell-Alternating-Press-on-Floor_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Alternating Press On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Kettlebell Alternating Press On Floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Press On Floor - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('e6be12cf-f746-474e-b0ce-bd1a854b26de', 'Single Leg Squat (pistol)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Squat (pistol) is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '7321201', '07321201-Single-Leg-Squat-(pistol)-(female)_Hips-FIX2_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e6c26fcf-a683-441f-95f2-abbdcb52f315', 'Stepback Floor Tap Diagonal Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '83951201', '83951201-Stepback-Floor-Tap-Diagonal-Reach-(male)_Plyometri.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Stepback Floor Tap Diagonal Reach. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback Floor Tap Diagonal Reach', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e6fb3a58-455e-4e12-afc2-65cc1c3e8278', 'Knees And Toes Point In Squat Slide (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Knees And Toes Point In Squat Slide Wall is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '89541201', '89541201-Knees-and-Toes-Point-In-Squat-Slide-Wall-(male)_Hi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Knees And Toes Point In Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e7004573-0092-4c0d-8eed-2b6e57144639', 'Palm Rotational Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, lats assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '26221201', '26221201-Dumbbell-Palm-Rotational-Bent-Over-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Palm Rotational Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bent_over_row', 'Palm Rotational Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e7007d8b-225c-4b3a-a1db-ee1670d1bb21', 'Walk (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Walk is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '72821201', '72821201-Resistance-Band-Walk-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Walk. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e709c9d7-e367-4e57-8368-70f9cbecc185', 'Bent Arm Lift', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '66901201', '66901201-Bent-Arm-Lift-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bent Arm Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Bent Arm Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e717f4a8-6d48-4ce6-bfca-ae91e777396c', 'Rounded Rollout (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '29371201', '29371201-Stability-Ball-Rounded-Rollout-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Stability Ball Rounded Rollout. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stability Ball Rounded Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Stability Ball Rounded Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e726e741-c650-42f4-93a1-1ec0e3852203', 'V Up Double Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '42721201', '42721201-V-up-Double-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. A solid choice for core day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'V Up Double Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e727bc87-68b2-4d54-8f80-fcdc6a133e4d', 'Single Arm Side Straight Arm Lat Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Side Straight Arm Lat Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '58441201', '58441201-Single-Arm-Side-Straight-Arm-Lat-Pulldown-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 2. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 3. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Single Arm Side Straight Arm Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e7291b1c-106c-4e7b-917d-406ad2ac2c1d', 'Explosive Kneeling Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Explosive Kneeling Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '67771201', '67771201-Explosive-Kneeling-Push-Up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Explosive Kneeling Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e72f4543-8ac3-4de0-949d-95c3f69c720f', 'Standing Scapular Rotation', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this rotation movement targeting your full body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '72331201', '72331201-Standing-Scapular-Rotation-(back-POV)-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Scapular Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Scapular Rotation', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e733f4d7-1248-4f36-b364-0be5ff97d141', 'Kneeling Finger Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '73211201', '73211201-Kneeling-Finger-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Kneeling Finger Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e757817b-9044-434b-97bd-cadf7be898fa', 'Incline Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Incline Hammer Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3201201', '03201201-Dumbbell-Incline-Hammer-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Hammer Curl', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e75a4a4e-e81f-43c3-8e13-491f68f7b4b5', 'Chin Up - Neutral Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Neutral Grip Chin Up is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Secondary activation of your biceps provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '80101201', '80101201-Neutral-Grip-Chin-Up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 2. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 3. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Chin Up - Neutral Grip', 'Chin Up - Neutral Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e7686887-ba8b-47e5-bb5a-539a28d57fc2', 'Cat Cow To Wide Downward Dog Calf Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cat Cow To Wide Downward Dog Calf Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The hamstrings, calves, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82181201', '82181201-Cat-Cow-to-Wide-Downward-Dog-Calf-Stretch-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cat Cow To Wide Downward Dog Calf Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_stretch', 'Cat Cow To Wide Downward Dog Calf Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e772b01a-562b-412e-944f-874a81489393', 'Split Squat (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '31111201', '31111201-Smith-Split-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Smith Split Squat', 'Split Squat', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e777aecd-ab19-4c8b-8d2f-e5822094f098', 'Jab Cross Slip Right Cross Left Hook (combo)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '104431201', '104431201-Jab-Cross-Slip-Right-Cross-Left-Hook-(combo)_Boxing.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jab Cross Slip Right Cross Left Hook. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Jab Cross Slip Right Cross Left Hook', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e77c228d-d6c8-42b7-b74c-1b3a88564760', 'Half Kneeling Single Arm Bottoms Up Press (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise engages your core for improved core stability and strength. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '44461201', '44461201-Kettlebell-Half-Kneeling-One-Arm-Bottoms-Up-Press_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Half Kneeling One Arm Bottoms Up Press. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Execute the pressing motion for Kettlebell Half Kneeling One Arm Bottoms Up Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bottoms_up', 'Half Kneeling Single Arm Bottoms Up Press', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('e7c39339-94d8-4ecb-b534-d5cb930ee8b8', 'Triceps Dip Floor To Table Top Plank (Dip Bars)', 'Arms', 'Dip Bars', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stabilization movement focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '102061201', '102061201-Triceps-Dip-Floor-to-Table-Top-Plank-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Triceps Dip Floor To Table Top Plank. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Triceps Dip Floor To Table Top Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e7c7a9ff-9b99-4486-b31f-2834d5cdc3ef', 'Lateral Raise (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '9071201', '09071201-Band-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e7e4436a-fd8a-40b0-af70-db8b7f913487', 'Kneeling Fire Hydrant Cross Knee Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. The hip abductors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '84921201', '84921201-Kneeling-Fire-Hydrant-Cross-Knee-Tap-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Fire Hydrant Cross Knee Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Kneeling Fire Hydrant Cross Knee Tap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('e7e6a140-55f8-49eb-bd6f-dacf463cde07', 'Wrist Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cable Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '2471201', '02471201-Cable-Wrist-Curl_Forearms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Wrist Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e7e7f6da-0972-44a7-ba73-9033d390cd43', 'Seated Wrist Extensors Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your wrists with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82451201', '82451201-Seated-Wrist-Extensors-Stretch-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Wrist Extensors Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Wrist Extensors Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e7ea18b7-c095-4562-b632-a29bdb1bb2ea', '4 Way Single Leg Hop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the 4 Way Single Leg Hop builds reactive power and improves conditioning. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '90661201', '90661201-4-Way-Single-Leg-Hop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 2. Set up in the starting position for 4 Way Single Leg Hop. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 45, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', '4 Way Single Leg Hop', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e7ef53e7-6b94-4177-a349-43e55020a576', 'V Sit (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '74441201', '74441201-V-Sit-against-Wall-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for V Sit Against Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'V Sit Against Wall', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8079032-2e3e-4006-ad00-a7b1b887f995', 'Standing Single Front Leg Circle Chair Supported (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '86361201', '86361201-Standing-Single-Front-Leg-Circle-Chair-Supported-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Standing Single Front Leg Circle Chair Supported (', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8095632-e5e1-447d-895e-ab24714eef8d', 'Good Morning (Hack Squat Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This squatting movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67331201', '67331201-Lever-Good-Morning-on-the-Hack-Squat-Machine-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Good Morning On The Hack Squat Machine. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'back_extension', 'Lever Good Morning On The Hack Squat', 'leg_press, squat, leg_extension', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e809ed4e-8adc-4054-b308-3fdfea7b8ca1', 'Plank Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this rowing movement that works your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74761201', '74761201-Dumbbell-Plank-Row-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plank Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'plank', 'Plank Row', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e80f2023-7c12-4a4f-b0c6-05c88afaf5bf', 'Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '6201201', '06201201-Lying-Leg-Raise-Flat-Bench_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Use a flat bench for this exercise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e82084b7-507b-45a7-8f60-4ab1c38baddc', 'Shuffle Air Bike (Air Bike)', 'Full Body', 'Air Bike', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '71691201', '71691201-Shuffle-Air-Bike-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shuffle Air Bike. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 35, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Shuffle Air Bike', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8232893-5c31-4248-af04-392ebd8c4ef1', 'Crunch (On Bench)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2701201', '02701201-Crunch-(on-bench)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8564066-3f05-42f8-a4bc-8807fefa44cd', 'Standing Two Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Standing Two Side Bend is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '32541201', '32541201-Standing-Two-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Two Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Two Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e85de626-fb22-4679-afd0-2d23082b7c0a', 'Clean And Press (Barbell)', 'Full Body', 'Barbell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Quads","Glutes","Traps","Hamstrings","Upper Back","Core"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Clean And Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your quads, glutes, traps working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '281201', '00281201-Barbell-Clean-and-Press_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Clean And Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Barbell Clean And Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Olympic Lift, Overhead Press', 'Push, Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'clean', 'Clean And Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('e85e2447-9f58-4edc-8fea-a3240c257c76', 'Standing Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '23901201', '23901201-Dumbbell-Standing-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Triceps Extension. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Standing Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e85f50c0-7e25-418e-9750-c3b9831ac68d', 'Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '1561201', '01561201-Cable-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e864c8ac-86fb-436d-9676-46c447898465', 'Kneeling Opposite Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Kneeling Opposite Shoulder Press is a flexibility exercise that targets your delts, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85021201', '85021201-Dumbbell-Kneeling-Opposite-Shoulder-Press-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Kneeling Opposite Shoulder Press. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Kneeling Opposite Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e87185dd-9488-459d-8d44-4a069de7b731', 'Backkick Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this kicking exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '84591201', '84591201-Backkick-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Backkick Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Backkick Side Step', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e875748e-4bd8-4712-92c4-e8cfa0ccb058', 'Side Squat (Towel)', 'Legs', 'Towel', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '67071201', '67071201-Bodyweight-Side-Squat-with-Towel-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. A solid choice for legs day.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat With Towel', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e877c083-a674-42b0-ba9b-82f113d7a41e', 'Side Step Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Row is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic rowing movements. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '84551201', '84551201-Side-Step-Row-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Step Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8878e59-a821-4f4c-a6ec-e48a6bc47233', 'Squat To Front Leg', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '45031201', '45031201-Bodyweight-Squat-to-Front-Leg_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat To Front Leg', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e88b3885-2871-40e7-bcac-8417c345131b', 'Mountain Climber Burpee', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity climbing exercise that challenges your entire body. Your hip flexors, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '74481201', '74481201-Mountain-Climber-Burpee-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Mountain Climber Burpee', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e88b391a-5e51-456b-870b-257b2dd54cd3', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focus (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Hyperextension Bench', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '79991201', '79991201-Resistance-Band-45-Degree-Hip-Extension-Glute-Focu.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focus. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Resistance Band 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focus. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focus', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('e88b5770-7764-4f32-a259-7c4700804ebd', 'Lying Roll Up Pilates', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Lying Roll Up Pilates provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '86961201', '86961201-Lying-Roll-Up-Pilates-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Roll Up Pilates. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Roll Up Pilates. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Roll Up Pilates', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e88cef13-f412-402b-80a8-80a1eaf3df61', 'Sled 45 Degrees Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7391201', '07391201-Sled-45-degrees-Leg-Press_Hips-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 2. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Sled 45 Degrees Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e896be8e-9055-41df-921b-c4da74422a59', 'Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '51151201', '51151201-Standing-Side-Crunch-Elbow-to-Knee-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. This exercise is excellent for abs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e89d6d68-59cc-4fcc-9825-28962d04f8e2', 'Lat Pulldown - Neutral Grip (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '75831201', '75831201-Cable-Neutral-Grip-Lat-Pulldown-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Neutral Grip Lat Pulldown. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lat Pulldown - Neutral Grip', 'Lat Pulldown - Neutral Grip', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('e8a5f4aa-8deb-4540-abbc-b850587e04fd', 'Chest Dip On Bench', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this dipping movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '54591201', '54591201-Chest-Dip-on-Bench_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Chest Dip On Bench', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8ab49c0-0963-4fec-bb0c-5196d4c4b64a', 'L Sit Rope Climb', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This climbing exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. You''ll also feel your biceps, core working to support the movement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '107311201', '107311201-L-Sit-Rope-Climb-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for L Sit Rope Climb. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rope_climb', 'L Sit Rope Climb', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8b16e8b-83d9-4014-9839-6e64ac422a84', 'Seated Calf Raise (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Calf Raise On A Chair isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '84291201', '84291201-Seated-Calf-Raise-on-a-Chair-(male)_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Seated Calf Raise On A Chair', 'calf_raise, standing_calf_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8be4c73-5813-4588-ba1f-633adff6f874', 'Arm Circle Stepback', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Arm Circle Stepback builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '56101201', '56101201-Arm-Circle-Stepback-(Male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Arm Circle Stepback. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Arm Circle Stepback', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8c75e6c-c24d-44e2-857e-63586a377c4a', 'Sliding Leg Curl On Floor (Towel) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Towel', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Alternating Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '101251201', '101251201-Alternating-Sliding-Leg-Curl-on-Floor-with-Towel-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Alternating Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Sliding Leg Curl On Floor With Towel - Alternating', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8d05263-6f4c-4702-bf10-e75e9fce3d60', 'Peterson Forward Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Peterson Forward Side Step is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '85381201', '85381201-Peterson-Forward-Side-Step-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Peterson Forward Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Peterson Forward Side Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e8e70e10-e30d-48cb-83bc-a26644371582', 'Bench Press (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Flat Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '7481201', '07481201-Smith-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Smith Bench Press', 'Bench Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e8fb4342-4545-4152-a000-35c4675a8482', 'Single Leg Squat Figure (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11361201', '11361201-Suspender-Single-Leg-Squat-(female)-(figure)_Thigh.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Single Leg Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Suspender Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e9109fad-0fb0-4b71-80e4-532f159376ba', 'Standing Single Leg Calf Rock', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your calves with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The standing position engages your core for stability. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '105471201', '105471201-Standing-Single-Leg-Calf-Rock-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Single Leg Calf Rock. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Single Leg Calf Rock', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e923547e-9aa5-4070-8e04-f2b340ceab83', 'Rear Delt And Back Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build balanced shoulders by working the posterior delts with this raising exercise. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '95391201', '95391201-Bodyweight-Rear-Delt-and-Back-Raise-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides and back, focusing on rear delts. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt And Back Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, face_pull, bent_over_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e932a044-acfc-455e-bff2-253db02458e7', 'Seated Arms Curl Stepout (Chair)', 'Arms', 'Chair', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity curling exercise that challenges your entire body. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '69061201', '69061201-Sitting-Arms-Curl-StepOut-on-a-Chair-(female)_Plyo.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Seated Arms Curl Stepout On A Chair', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e932db99-8293-46ac-ba64-2441e099586b', 'Side Shuffle Forward Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '72711201', '72711201-Side-Shuffle-Forward-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Shuffle Forward Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Side Shuffle Forward Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9425b17-d021-4089-8fb0-6ef4b0a2a030', 'Kneeling Abdominal Draw In', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '70571201', '70571201-Kneeling-Abdominal-Draw-In-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Abdominal Draw In. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Abdominal Draw In', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e960817b-c573-4f3a-bd00-6a8e6b7fb234', 'Roll Lower Back (side) Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '54221201', '54221201-Roll-Lower-Back-(Side)-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Bac.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Lower BackLying On Floor. 2. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Roll Lower Back Lying On Floor', 'Roll Lower Back Lying On Floor', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e96255e1-e464-4a9e-a8a7-5c4ccdf5544b', 'Arnold Press II (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '2871201', '02871201-Dumbbell-Arnold-Press-II_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Arnold Press II. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Arnold Press II', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('e98416c7-c68d-47b9-a1bd-d873a5e89809', 'Side Step Reverse Fly', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Reverse Fly is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic flying movements. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '98541201', '98541201-Side-Step-Reverse-Fly-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Perfect for targeting your full body. Variation: Side Step Reverse Fly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Side Step Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e98a81af-e396-4af0-934d-cbded48b8f4a', 'Side Step Knee Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '80371201', '80371201-Side-Step-Knee-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Knee Reach. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Step Knee Reach', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e98d503e-4a8b-4463-aa2f-e5913256faa9', 'Bodyweight Shift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '90601201', '90601201-Bodyweight-Shift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Shift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bodyweight Shift', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9a41740-830b-4422-8215-c2381af23e49', 'Double Pigeon Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hips, the Double Pigeon Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '58901201', '58901201-Double-Pigeon-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Double Pigeon Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Double Pigeon Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9a6d4da-7750-4e9a-80ee-874cbcbc6d1c', 'Spiderman Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this pushing movement focusing on your chest. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11381201', '11381201-Suspender-Spiderman-Push-up-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Spiderman Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Spiderman Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('e9baa36b-8c97-4b3e-bf1a-d81f6113d75a', 'Side Squat Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '46481201', '46481201-Bodyweight-Side-Squat-Step-(female)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat Step', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9cfb209-ce45-47b9-9d24-453500efa9c0', 'Brachialis Narrow Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Brachialis Narrow Pull Up is an arm rowing exercise targeting your lats. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '106951201', '106951201-Brachialis-Narrow-Pull-up-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Brachialis Narrow Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9da306f-20f1-4446-b978-5063c51e75f8', 'Assisted Chin Up (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lever Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Lever Assisted Chin Up is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '5721201', '05721201-Lever-Assisted-Chin-Up_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Assisted Chin Up. 2. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 3. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Lever Assisted Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e9e3c378-10b0-411d-a3a0-5bd9ed98df66', 'Front Pulldown (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lat Pulldown Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Lever Front Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '70711201', '70711201-Lever-Front-Pulldown-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Front Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Front Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('e9ec2f92-b84e-4049-a4f7-c433995b77bf', 'Rear Lunge Kickback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '74331201', '74331201-Rear-Lunge-Kickback-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Rear Lunge Kickback', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9fd6aa9-a968-4efc-8e75-dff72b495e74', 'Sumo Squat With Heel Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '105231201', '105231201-Sumo-Squat-with-Heel-Raise-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Sumo Squat With Heel Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Sumo Squat With Heel Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('e9fe3864-e0b6-4614-8a82-c69758c62a9f', 'Lying Cross Ankle Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '59391201', '59391201-Lying-Cross-Ankle-Tap-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Cross Ankle Tap. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Cross Ankle Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Lying Cross Ankle Tap', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea06df57-6307-4d6b-a44c-c4ec8e16b377', 'Half Kneeling Single Arm Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '76181201', '76181201-Cable-Half-Kneeling-Single-Arm-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Half Kneeling Single Arm Row. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Half Kneeling Single Arm Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ea4372fb-11b4-4cf0-8982-60c6b78b2108', 'Split Jump Twist Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Split Jump Twist Row is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic rowing movements. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '76451201', '76451201-Split-Jump-Twist-Row-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge_jump', 'Split Jump Twist Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea455a8d-4ee8-4bca-a659-f12130b86a24', 'Ring Isometric Hold Reverse Ab Rollout (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Ring Isometric Hold Reverse Ab Rollout, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your lats, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '93131201', '93131201-Ring-Isometric-Hold-Reverse-Ab-Rollout_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Ring Isometric Hold Reverse Ab Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 33, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Ring Isometric Hold Reverse Ab Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ea47dfcc-0986-4e3e-826d-2822979c084e', 'Seated Scapular Adduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Scapular Adduction is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '69141201', '69141201-Sitting-Scapular-Adduction-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Scapular Adduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Seated Scapular Adduction', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea6b07c6-31ea-4c11-a7ce-00e80c2d00db', 'Prisoner Get Up', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Prisoner Get Up, a comprehensive movement exercise. Secondary activation of your quads, core provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '43881201', '43881201-Prisoner-Get-Up_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Prisoner Get Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'turkish_getup', 'Prisoner Get Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea756fa8-ea5d-4140-b746-aaecb44a1289', 'Run', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '6851201', '06851201-Run_Cardio.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Run. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Run', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea787b2f-c9aa-44ae-a8de-5ca646cde758', 'Seated Knee Flexion (Resistance Band, Chair)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This full-body flexion exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '92731201', '92731201-Resistance-Band-Sitting-Knee-Flexion-on-a-Chair-(f.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Knee Flexion On A Chair. 2. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Knee Flexion On A Chair', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ea7fab07-9cca-452a-a1d6-58f6ee3c2bc5', 'Seated Figure Four Rock', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your glutes area and enhance overall flexibility. Your hips work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '96721201', '96721201-Sitting-Figure-Four-Rock-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Figure Four Rock. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Seated Figure Four Rock', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea80b241-690d-4d30-9a25-3e197a54eaf4', 'Incline Pronated Grip Front Raise (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your front delts. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '96511201', '96511201-Barbell-Incline-Pronated-Grip-Front-Raise_Shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Pronated Grip Front Raise. 2. Use an overhand (pronated) grip with palms facing down/away. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Incline Pronated Grip Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ea82c3b7-106d-42e5-b775-e5a9b938f676', 'Bicep Curl - Single Arm 45 Degrees (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Band 45 Degrees One Arm Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '59281201', '59281201-Band-45-degrees-One-Arm-Biceps-Curl-(male)_Upper-arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band 45 Degrees One Arm Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', '45 Degrees Single Arm Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ea84be81-fae1-40d9-bb4c-6813ca389f74', 'Kneeling Backwards Reach', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your back area and enhance overall flexibility. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '78891201', '78891201-Kneeling-Backwards-Reach-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Backwards Reach. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Kneeling Backwards Reach', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea8ae700-f22f-413b-bc64-2abe62c83032', 'Scapula Dip', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Scapula Dips is a dipping exercise that develops back strength and muscle. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '39371201', '39371201-Scapula-Dips-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. An effective movement for your back routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Scapula Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ea8d1498-9349-4690-9aa3-3ba4f118a9e7', 'Lying Crossover Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stretching exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93601201', '93601201-Lying-Crossover-Stretch-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crossover Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Crossover Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lying Crossover Stretch', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eaa51ba2-c8d0-42b6-8163-789c23f90adb', 'March On Spot Arm Circles', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Aim for full range of motion on every rep. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '79481201', '79481201-March-on-Spot-Arm-Circles-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for March On Spot Arm Circles. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'March On Spot Arm Circles', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eabcbae1-9317-4046-961d-9b65a16b88b9', 'Sweep March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '52941201', '52941201-Sweep-March-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sweep March. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Sweep March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eada3d2a-5375-4112-92b3-592e9000177a', 'T Bar Row - Reverse Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever T Bar Reverse Grip Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. You''ll also feel your biceps, lats working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '13511201', '13511201-Lever-T-Bar-Reverse-Grip-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever T Bar Reverse Grip Row. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 't_bar_row', 'Lever T Bar Row - Reverse Grip', 'Lever T Bar Row - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('eade6f36-0007-4561-9b9b-2118f229d27b', 'Prone W Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Dumbbell Prone W Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '77471201', '77471201-Dumbbell-Prone-W-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone W Raise. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone W Raise. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Prone W Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Prone W Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eaf4ba8a-3524-4f40-9b00-b014a6a28f53', 'Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this stretching movement focusing on your delts. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '78661201', '78661201-Shoulder-Stretch-Behind-the-Back-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eaf783af-6943-4b74-902f-43c2d5a2d18f', 'Seated Triceps Extension (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '4531201', '04531201-EZ-Barbell-Seated-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Seated Triceps Extension. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'EZ Seated Triceps Extension', 'EZ Seated Triceps Extension', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('eb0e56c3-ad13-4b73-97e0-860323afaa65', 'Reverse Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this curling exercise. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3851201', '03851201-Dumbbell-Reverse-Wrist-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Reverse Wrist Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Reverse Wrist Curl', 'hammer_curl, wrist_curl, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eb119fbb-ab98-49bf-9a55-6a82a0568d31', 'Hip Circles Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Hip Circles Stretch provides a deep stretch for your hips, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '18471201', '18471201-Hip-Circles-Stretch-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Hip Circles Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Hip Circles Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb1b36da-27a7-4b80-bcea-8b1c4c7481c0', 'Crunchy Frog On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '35101201', '35101201-Crunchy-Frog-on-Floor_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Crunchy Frog On Floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunchy Frog On Floor', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb1c1d76-769d-4ba0-a337-ce983615fc33', 'Finger Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '4551201', '04551201-Barbell-Finger-Curls_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Finger Curls. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Finger Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('eb1e3f19-2dbb-4593-811d-8d394bfec54c', 'Lying Side Reverse Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Side Reverse Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '73761201', '73761201-Lying-Side-Reverse-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 3. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lying Side Reverse Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb234f93-ba02-4fcc-8bf5-a0ddb03a41d0', 'Standing Plate Press (Plate)', 'Chest', 'Weight Plate', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Plate Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '12251201', '12251201-Standing-Plate-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Plate Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb267320-0921-4c92-9ed2-1c0111d7d2dc', 'Over Bench Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Over Bench Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3691201', '03691201-Dumbbell-Over-Bench-Wrist-Curl_Forearms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Over Bench Wrist Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Over Bench Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eb473f03-ecbc-47ef-911c-b36c02abad04', 'Clean (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Glutes","Traps"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Dumbbell Clean, a comprehensive movement exercise. Your quads, glutes, traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '2951201', '02951201-Dumbbell-Clean_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Clean. 2. Explosively pull the weight upward from the starting position. 3. Pull yourself under the weight and catch it at shoulder level. 4. Stand to complete the lift, then lower with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'clean', 'Clean', 'power_clean, deadlift, front_squat', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eb544513-7287-4dc6-8c20-d619642f9613', 'Standing Y Raise - Rope (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '83201201', '83201201-Cable-Standing-Y-raises-(with-rope-attachment)-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Y Raises. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Cable Standing Y Raises. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('eb5f9029-31d2-4357-b529-67024cfeb5f7', 'Incline Palm In Press (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Kettlebell Incline Palm In Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '68231201', '68231201-Kettlebell-Incline-Palm-in-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Incline Palm In Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Incline Palm In Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('eb6216f9-af53-4025-9ef9-3065fe180580', 'Decline Shrug (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Traps","Upper Back"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '74051201', '74051201-Dumbbell-Decline-Shrug-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Shrug', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Decline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eb68fcc7-9045-4bfe-a037-b5817620135d', 'Seated Pulse Back Squeeze', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Pulse Back Squeeze is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '51321201', '51321201-Seated-Pulse-Back-Squeeze-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Seated Pulse Back Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb696a17-f30c-44e7-a9dd-10178fdb9578', 'Seated Wrist Rotation (Chair)', 'Arms', 'Chair', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this rotation exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '90921201', '90921201-Sitting-Wrist-Rotation-on-a-Chair-(female)_Forearm.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Wrist Rotation On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_stretch', 'Seated Wrist Rotation On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb6a54e5-f136-439e-a043-56e70b36494a', 'Plank Feet Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Plank Feet Tap is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '49271201', '49271201-Plank-Feet-Tap_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Beneficial for overall core development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Feet Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb78a932-3089-4f27-8786-251bb6a19bfb', 'Walk The Dog', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walk The Dog is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61301201', '61301201-Walk-The-Dog-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Walk The Dog. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Walk The Dog', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb794cc5-bdbe-4a90-bb49-8b4caa94b28a', 'Walking On Spot Small Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic kicking movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '90541201', '90541201-Walking-on-Spot-Small-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot Small Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Spot Small Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eb9ab35b-1f3b-4350-bf48-f7010dfdd4fb', 'Side Step Pushdown', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Pushdown is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic pushing movements. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97801201', '97801201-Side-Step-Pushdown-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Side Step Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebb46cfc-97a5-482c-a3a5-2ffd840d99e7', 'Rack Pull (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell, Power Rack', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Rack Pull targets your hamstrings through a controlled pulling motion. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '741201', '00741201-Barbell-Rack-Pull_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Rack Pull. 2. Set up in the starting position for Barbell Rack Pull. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Hip Hinge', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Rack Pull', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ebbc3485-a9c5-4834-94a8-f20edf8c4e04', 'Squat To Toe Stretch Plantar Flexion', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Squat To Toe Stretch Plantar Flexion helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '83881201', '83881201-Squat-to-Toe-Stretch-Plantar-Flexion-(female)_Stre.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 75, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Squat To Toe Stretch Plantar Flexion', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebcb3aa9-0f00-4c40-a99d-94f11902b31c', 'Seated Side Bend Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Seated Side Bend Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your obliques, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Secondary activation of your lats, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '85011201', '85011201-Sitting-Side-Bend-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side Bend Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Seated Side Bend Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebcb9cf8-32a9-4e8a-a6bb-2363e182ac98', 'Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '11281201', '11281201-Suspender-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ebcdaf29-7776-4950-9bad-36bdacc85898', 'Bench Seated Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Bench Seated Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '74061201', '74061201-Dumbbell-Bench-Seated-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bench Seated Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Bench Seated Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ebd4b9f8-15e3-46b6-8908-1a721fc6dd0d', 'Single Arm High Scapular Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '65111201', '65111201-Cable-Single-Arm-High-Scapular-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Single Arm High Scapular Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ebddd317-cac1-4ccc-8bfa-044d11e5cfd1', 'Incline Push Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '18511201', '18511201-Incline-Push-Press_Chest-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Incline Push Press', 'bench_press, chest_fly, shoulder_press, decline_bench_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebde6f8d-beae-4934-a195-edf6d88c8a97', 'Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '22221201', '22221201-Dumbbell-Romanian-Deadlift-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ebe565e4-42de-4e40-90f4-1908df9ab36d', 'Assisted Isometric Core (Stick)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '53991201', '53991201-Stick-Assisted-Isometric-Core-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stick Assisted Isometric Core. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Stick Assisted Isometric Core', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebf17531-a249-4a4b-a31f-1f121f5423ba', 'Seating Leg Abduction And Extension - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hips"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this extension movement focusing on your hip abductors. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '90721201', '90721201-Seating-Alternate-Leg-Abduction-and-Extension-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 2. Lower with control back to the starting position. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Seating Leg Abduction And Extension - Alternating', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ebfe21b0-983b-4554-b7d2-d8c8b5c247dd', 'Chin Up Izometric And Negative (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Chin Up (izometric And Negative) is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '47251201', '47251201-Chin-up-(izometric-and-negative)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec1732c7-d49c-428f-8c57-d0d5979ba2e0', 'Sumo Deadlift High Pull_thighs', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Lower Back","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Sumo Deadlift High Pull_thighs, an effective shoulder pulling exercise. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '11991201', '11991201-Sumo-Deadlift-High-Pull_Thighs_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 2. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 3. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'Sumo Deadlift High Pull_thighs', 'deadlift, squat, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('ec18ec46-c252-447c-a15b-1f168997b312', 'Lying Half Butterfly Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your delts. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '85251201', '85251201-Lying-Half-Butterfly-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Half Butterfly Raise. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Lying Half Butterfly Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec2b9e36-cf00-4993-8795-9fb4ecf4af83', 'Seated Hamstrings Stretch (Chair) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings, Chair', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Target your hamstrings with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '82861201', '82861201-Seated-Alternate-Hamstrings-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Alternate Hamstrings Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Hamstrings Stretch On A Chair - Alternating', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ec2f48d9-c7c5-4d6f-a917-50677c347414', 'Side Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74341201', '74341201-Side-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Works well for quads activation.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec37223a-879a-4607-b60c-41c5c501bb8f', 'Standing Single Arm Circle (Against Wall)', 'Shoulders', 'Wall', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your delts. The standing position engages your core for stability. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '95371201', '95371201-Standing-Single-Arm-Circle-on-a-Wall-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 39, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Single Arm Circle On A Wall', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec525323-a1e5-4680-972a-2081ef7dbe89', 'Rear Lunge From Deficit (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine, Step Platform', '{Quadriceps}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '88011201', '88011201-Smith-Rear-Lunge-from-Deficite-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Rear Lunge From Deficite. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Smith Rear Lunge From Deficite', 'Rear Lunge From Deficite', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ec56a07f-9ca8-46e5-bd44-168729d3d88e', 'Double Hip Rotation Cross Knee Drive', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Double Hip Rotation Cross Knee Drive builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '74851201', '74851201-Double-Hip-Rotation-Cross-Knee-Drive-(female)_Plyo.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Double Hip Rotation Cross Knee Drive. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Double Hip Rotation Cross Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec5b341c-e212-4a3e-8342-7c4d0670d19c', 'Incline Rear Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Dumbbell Incline Rear Lateral Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3261201', '03261201-Dumbbell-Incline-Rear-Lateral-Raise_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Rear Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Incline Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ec5b62b1-7540-406d-8b8d-28fdba7b04f0', 'Forearm Wall Slide (Wall)', 'Shoulders', 'Wall', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your rotator cuff. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '29411201', '29411201-Forearm-Wall-Slide_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Forearm Wall Slide. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your rotator cuff. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'serratus', 'Forearm Wall Slide', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec6e19bd-2ba6-486b-a47a-5a1baabcde03', 'Incline Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '25071201', '25071201-Dumbbell-Incline-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Incline Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ec756da5-2fef-4a5a-a73e-f2fc18896b38', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest High Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing Straight Arm Chest High Fly is a flying exercise that targets your chest muscles. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '83521201', '83521201-Bodyweight-Standing-Straight-Arm-Chest-High-Fly-(m.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest High Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec7dd5ba-b407-4497-afa8-e51daaf56776', 'Toe Side Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted stepping exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '107621201', '107621201-Toe-Side-Walk_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Toe Side Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Toe Side Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ec9d3e85-3792-416a-a5d4-d9f01d4d3d24', 'Leg Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Extension Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this extension movement that develops leg drive and power. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '22561201', '22561201-Lever-Leg-Extension-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Leg Extension. 2. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 3. Lower with control back to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Lever Leg Extension', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('eca1c0ab-9969-44f7-8a41-00e43bf2d920', 'High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a pulling motion. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '30471201', '30471201-Cable-High-Pulley-Overhead-Tricep-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('eca49971-7949-44d8-a957-ef5ff9eae613', 'Lying Toe Tap - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Alternate Toe Tap is a lower body movement exercise that targets your full body. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '76991201', '76991201-Lying-Alternate-Toe-Tap-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternate Toe Tap. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Toe Tap - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eca56e4b-075b-46b0-9a6b-9d2887af2cff', 'Roll Kneeling Upper Back Rotation', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this rotation movement targeting your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '54331201', '54331201-Roll-Kneeling-Upper-Back-Rotation-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Roll Kneeling Upper Back Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Roll Kneeling Upper Back Rotation', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ecad9c00-5102-47d4-bb41-d82dcc5d4a61', 'Lying Face Pull (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pulling movement focusing on your delts. Your upper back, rotator cuff work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '75911201', '75911201-Cable-Lying-Face-Pull-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Face Pull. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Face Pull. 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Lying Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ecb32f04-97af-45f2-b424-e78430ae7730', 'Walking Arms Kickback', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Walking Arms Kickback is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic kicking movements. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '99141201', '99141201-Walking-Arms-Kickback-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 2. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Walking Arms Kickback', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ecca5b9f-1785-42fe-8e75-a9644fc860b8', 'Single Arm Jerk (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Kettlebell One Arm Jerk, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '5381201', '05381201-Kettlebell-One-Arm-Jerk_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell One Arm Jerk. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jerk', 'Single Arm Jerk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('ece17609-3fa9-40d4-b553-dcaace16bc3c', 'Mini Hip Lift (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Mini Hip Lift On A Chair is a hip-dominant movement exercise that targets your glutes. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '82831201', '82831201-Mini-Hip-Lift-on-a-Chair-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up in the starting position for Mini Hip Lift On A Chair. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Mini Hip Lift On A Chair', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eceee950-89bf-4e05-9166-772e0de99923', 'Incline Single Arm Chest Press (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Lever Incline Single Arm Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '88061201', '88061201-Lever-Incline-Single-Arm-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Incline Single Arm Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 76, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Incline Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ecfa492e-d1f8-4267-a38d-1c77a809d7e7', 'Brettzel With Head Turn', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '79071201', '79071201-Brettzel-with-Head-Turn-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Brettzel With Head Turn. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Brettzel With Head Turn', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ecfffc84-ce66-46f5-b435-0ef1befb4784', 'Crunch (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Crunch Against Wall is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '74141201', '74141201-Crunch-against-Wall-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch Against Wall', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed03900a-f7c2-4992-8ff9-39396bb11419', 'Seated Arm Circle (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Arm Circle On A Chair is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '90901201', '90901201-Sitting-Arm-Circle-on-a-Chair-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. A solid choice for shoulders day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Seated Arm Circle On A Chair', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed0bc8e5-b1e6-4163-8f35-dc80bba30be1', 'Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your lateral delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '56311201', '56311201-Dumbbell-Standing-Bent-Arm-Lateral-raise-(male)_Sh.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ed19b788-7db9-4845-91d5-9a5096a3eba5', 'Single Leg Extension Crunch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Extension Crunch is a core extension exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '72581201', '72581201-Single-Leg-Extension-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 2. Lower with control back to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Single Leg Extension Crunch', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed245f95-00a4-4a66-a9f6-122e1d6c4e55', 'Around The World Lying On Floor', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your delts. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '63051201', '63051201-Around-the-World-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Around The World Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Around The World Lying On Floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, 'Static', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, 'Neutral', 'Narrow', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Around The World Lying On Floor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed2add2c-fb40-4fbd-97d7-4281837667f5', 'Power Up Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic jumping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your quads, calves provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '80301201', '80301201-Power-Up-Jump-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 2. Set up in the starting position for Power Up Jump. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Power Up Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed37b0ee-8741-4686-84d2-5e1a0c345f73', 'Rear Lunge Front Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '56201201', '56201201-Bodyweight-Rear-Lunge-Front-Raise-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Rear Lunge Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed392c39-1fdb-4072-8e76-11b7bb2b68d7', 'Squat Royalty Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '104151201', '104151201-Dumbbell-Squat-Royalty-Lunge-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Squat Royalty Lunge. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Squat Royalty Lunge', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ed3b53c7-3677-445d-8c4d-ca4180836a95', 'Lying Floor Horizontal Flutter Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Floor Horizontal Flutter Kick is a lower body kicking exercise that targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '93211201', '93211201-Lying-Floor-Horizontal-Flutter-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Floor Horizontal Flutter Kick. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Floor Horizontal Flutter Kick. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Floor Horizontal Flutter Kick', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed3b9648-ade6-4ba6-9246-e6981d123e58', 'Push Up - Close Grip (On Knees)', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The chest, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '26131201', '26131201-Close-grip-Push-up-(on-knees)-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up - Close Grip', 'Push Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed50b360-fbd0-4689-9d5c-68c5989918fe', 'Reverse Preacher Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '101741201', '101741201-Dumbbell-Reverse-Preacher-Curl-(female)_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Reverse Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. An effective movement for your arms routine.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Reverse Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ed57f588-838f-4416-a20b-14325edc6dcd', 'Rear Drive (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This movement movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Your rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '30591201', '30591201-Cable-Rear-Drive-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Rear Drive. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Rear Drive. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Rear Drive', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ed5ae033-786f-4634-893e-dad15204f57a', 'Criss Cross Arms Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '66311201', '66311201-Criss-Cross-Arms-Lift-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Criss Cross Arms Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Arms Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed5c8ef5-9aef-41c6-b656-a5469e79a5d1', 'Lying Extension (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '39401201', '39401201-Dumbbell-Lying-Alternate-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Alternate Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Alternate Extension. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Dumbbell Lying Alternate Extension. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Extension - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ed6764b2-c8b0-410e-9b79-c2c09498a129', 'Abdominal Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Abdominal Stretch is a core stretching exercise that primarily targets your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '32441201', '32441201-Abdominal-Stretch-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Abdominal Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Abdominal Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed73bd2a-a4e3-492a-b84f-9fc997bdab2c', 'Standing Leg Lift Lat Pulldown (Cable) - Alternating', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '89201201', '89201201-Standing-Alternate-Leg-Lift-Lat-Pulldown-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Standing Leg Lift Lat Pulldown - Alternating', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ed7424c8-fac7-4e93-a8b6-7c3a20503f03', 'Standing Hip Saggital Rotation With Shoulders Tran', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Standing Hip Saggital Rotation With Shoulders Tran, a comprehensive rotation exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '53211201', '53211201-Standing-Hip-Saggital-Rotation-with-Shoulders-Tran.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Hip Saggital Rotation With Shoulders Tran. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Hip Saggital Rotation With Shoulders Tran', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed78ff52-2f1d-491c-995f-0ce9d0fa064d', 'Side Shuffle Overhead Punches', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '74951201', '74951201-Side-Shuffle-Overhead-Punches-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Shuffle Overhead Punches. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Side Shuffle Overhead Punches', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed7f2999-e297-472b-bd9c-5d67f150afba', 'Seated Single Arm Shoulder Press (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Shoulder Press Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Single Arm Shoulder Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '86931201', '86931201-Lever-Seated-Single-Arm-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Arm Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Lever Seated Single Arm Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ed81c3aa-ab01-4037-8561-c877927051d2', 'Staggered Stance Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Staggered Stance Romanian Deadlift targets your hamstrings through a controlled hip hinge motion. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '87221201', '87221201-Dumbbell-Staggered-Stance-Romanian-Deadlift-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Staggered Stance Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Staggered Stance Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ed90de4e-034e-4c57-b054-9e555a4e7cbc', 'Seated Chin Tuck (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Chin Tuck On A Chair targets your neck muscles through a controlled movement motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '92631201', '92631201-Sitting-Chin-Tuck-on-a-Chair-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. Great for building strength in your neck.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Chin Tuck On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed94cba2-9599-4e30-878f-9149ce4b5e5d', 'Front Plank Side Hop', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stabilization exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '37501201', '37501201-Front-Plank-Side-Hop-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Side Hop', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ed95e131-6cc7-457e-985b-3ddcfd5b57ef', 'Standing Elbows Nudge - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '94191201', '94191201-Standing-Alternating-Elbows-Nudge-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Elbows Nudge - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edae914f-a99b-4674-abee-4fc9622cfb6c', 'Standing Twist Air Bike', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '84041201', '84041201-Standing-Twist-Air-Bike-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Twist Air Bike. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 37, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Twist Air Bike', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edb405db-42d7-4e20-9fa5-d4249f689031', 'Lying Leg Hip Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Leg Hip Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '24471201', '24471201-Lying-leg-hip-raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Hip Raise. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Leg Hip Raise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Leg Hip Raise', 'squat, leg_curl, calf_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edb8bb31-8e89-4794-8767-48040434ede7', 'Preacher Curl - Reverse Grip (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Preacher Curl Machine', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '16161201', '16161201-Lever-Reverse-Grip-Preacher-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Reverse Grip Preacher Curl. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Lever Preacher Curl - Reverse Grip', 'Lever Preacher Curl - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('edbd7cf6-9717-4af7-a00a-ebf1a342432a', 'Lying (prone) Abdominal Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '11681201', '11681201-Lying-(prone)-Abdominal-Stretch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Set up in the starting position for LyingAbdominal Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying  Abdominal Stretch', 'Lying Abdominal Stretch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edbd8ba9-58e1-4bb2-83f5-0d4c47fac608', 'Plank Butt', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '23581201', '23581201-Plank---Butt-(WRONG-RIGHT)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Butt', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edd3760f-b1ec-432c-a7ed-1adf8ea9a094', 'Decline Bench Press - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '361201', '00361201-Barbell-Decline-Wide-Grip-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Decline Wide Grip Press. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Decline Press - Wide Grip', 'Decline Press - Wide Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('eddcc2dd-6114-495d-ba43-679bd92cf9c6', 'Squat Leg Lift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '61121201', '61121201-Squat-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Great for building strength in your quads. Variation: Squat Leg Lift.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Leg Lift', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ede3244b-aca4-4acb-957a-0e3631b18156', 'Weighted Front Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '8341201', '08341201-Weighted-Front-Raise_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Weighted Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edf6d415-4b11-4228-ae3c-3d0b34362e12', 'Side Crab Walk Back Fly', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity flying exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '84631201', '84631201-Side-Crab-Walk-Back-Fly-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Side Crab Walk Back Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('edfab6d2-4d3d-4b04-91a4-97372301a2ef', 'Side Step Squat Pick And Carry', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '68941201', '68941201-Side-Step-Squat-Pick-and-Carry-(female)_Plyometric.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Step Squat Pick And Carry', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee027634-7b41-4076-a453-66ccca40085d', 'Bottoms Up Single Arm Overhead Carry (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint movement movement. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '96971201', '96971201-Kettlebell-Bottoms-Up-Single-Arm-Overhead-Carry_We.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Bottoms Up Single Arm Overhead Carry. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'farmer_carry', 'Bottoms Up Single Arm Overhead Carry', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('ee09ba4c-92ab-4cd0-91ee-9ebabab004f0', 'Pull Through (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '10871201', '10871201-Suspender-Pull-Through-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Pull Through. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Pull Through. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_through', 'Suspender Pull Through', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ee0c06eb-bfb9-4c47-88ab-5d188acb7eec', 'Chest Press (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Suspension Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '57381201', '57381201-Suspension-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspension Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Suspension Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ee19763b-d6df-4a0b-b3b6-17a6f2df2693', 'Standing Front Raise - (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your front delts. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '3101201', '03101201-Dumbbell-Front-Raise_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee1f8867-8f7c-4a01-910f-a44173b4420b', 'Heel Elevated Bulgarian Split Squat (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75511201', '75511201-Bodyweight-Heel-Elevated-Bulgarian-Split-Squat-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Heel Elevated Bulgarian Split Squat', 'split_squat, lunge, leg_press', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee2142f9-a453-45e6-b6ca-9f22ac216f5e', 'Silent Burpee (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '105091201', '105091201-Silent-Burpee-with-Chair-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 3. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 4. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 35, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Silent Burpee With Chair', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee21b903-3679-48b0-bad5-6289eb9e6731', 'Devils Press (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Dumbbell Devils Press builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '41641201', '41641201-Dumbbell-Devils-Press_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Devils Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Devils Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Devils Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee309863-c281-4ed3-85d8-98a0ca5beb1f', '45 Degree Twisting Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11711201', '11711201-45-degree-twisting-hyperextension_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Hip Hinge / Trunk Extension', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degree Twisting Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee3134e7-11df-4b4e-8118-1ad2ab7d55d2', 'Overhead Crunch (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '83291201', '83291201-Dumbbell-Overhead-Crunch-(on-stability-ball)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Overhead Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 66, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Overhead Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee32b863-8021-41ec-99a7-6d7dc4a1cb80', 'Ab Mat Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Ab Mat Sit Up, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '65551201', '65551201-Ab-Mat-Sit-Up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ab Mat Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Ab Mat Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee3dd7c4-c1cc-47a8-8ef4-611eb7523295', 'Standing Wide Good Morning', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Standing Wide Good Morning provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '89681201', '89681201-Standing-Wide-Good-Morning-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Wide Good Morning. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Standing Wide Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee3ff362-2395-4189-8e45-9224b27ab6d3', 'Arms Swing Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic kicking movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '85191201', '85191201-Arms-Swing-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Arms Swing Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee49040d-f08c-4087-bb5d-55ffd6204202', 'Standing Hip Extension (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Band Standing Hip Extension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '9221201', '09221201-Band-standing-hip-extension-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Hip Extension. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Band Standing Hip Extension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ee4c7824-b29c-46d6-a565-88b63a65cc30', 'Lay Down Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Lay Down Push Up, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '60291201', '60291201-Lay-Down-Push-Up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Lay Down Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee548c64-0213-4fd4-a544-5dcb161ce4b7', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This full-body movement exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '34061201', '34061201-Standing-Pelvic-Tilt-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Pelvic Tilt. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee550c82-a84c-4b08-9ff3-e21bbe66ddc5', 'Zercher Back Extension (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this extension movement focusing on your lower back. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '89911201', '89911201-Barbell-Zercher-Back-Extension-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Zercher Back Extension. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Zercher Back Extension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ee64e305-f678-42a6-a878-e5ffc4d4560f', 'Lying Bench Poliquin Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '107371201', '107371201-Dumbbell-Lying-Bench-Poliquin-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Bench Poliquin Fly. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Bench Poliquin Fly. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lying Bench Poliquin Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee64ee77-e28c-4592-b2fb-715a1ceb77dd', 'Legs Side Pull In Sit Up (EZ Bar)', 'Core', 'EZ Bar', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '41871201', '41871201-EZ-Bar-Legs-Side-Pull-In-Sit-up_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Set up in the starting position for EZ Bar Legs Side Pull In Sit Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'EZ Bar Legs Side Pull In Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ee7128dd-9dc0-4b0e-94ad-53a52894dbaa', 'Sphinx Heel Drop', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '85501201', '85501201-Sphinx-Heel-Drop-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Sphinx Heel Drop. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Sphinx Heel Drop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee80cda7-c225-46d3-be4a-34560a316781', 'Twisting Crunch With Legs Supported (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Twisting Crunch With Legs Supported is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '104031201', '104031201-Dumbbell-Twisting-Crunch-with-Legs-Supported-(mal.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Twisting Crunch With Legs Supported. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Twisting Crunch With Legs Supported', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee8b763b-5597-4764-92dc-161a04786800', 'Feet And Ankles Rotation Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Feet And Ankles Rotation Stretch isolates your calf muscles through a rotation motion. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '42831201', '42831201-Feet-and-Ankles-Rotation-Stretch-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Feet And Ankles Rotation Stretch. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Feet And Ankles Rotation Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ee8f58fc-c69e-4035-b850-c9b9802e0451', 'Inverted Row - Wide Grip (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Wide Grip Inverted Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '44501201', '44501201-Suspender-Wide-Grip-Inverted-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Wide Grip Inverted Row. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Suspender Inverted Row - Wide Grip', 'Suspender Inverted Row - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ee964ff3-c050-4410-a81c-ff1c472451e8', 'Twisting Crunch Legs On Bench (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '103951201', '103951201-Dumbbell-Twisting-Crunch-Legs-on-Bench-(male)_Wai.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Twisting Crunch Legs On Bench. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Twisting Crunch Legs On Bench', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ee9a4c66-3531-4a4a-9ce5-7521fea19472', 'Decline Bench Press - Close Grip (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Decline Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '94001201', '94001201-Smith-Decline-Close-Grip-Bench-Press-(male)_Upper-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Decline Close Grip Bench Press. 2. Set the bench to a decline angle and secure your feet. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 5. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 96, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'close_grip_bench', 'Smith Decline Bench Press - Close Grip', 'Decline Bench Press - Close Grip', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ee9fb40d-6d59-43c5-a063-34cbb8581f51', 'PVC Pass Through', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '46071201', '46071201-PVC-Pass-Through_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for PVC Pass Through. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pass_through', 'PVC Pass Through', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eeb7fb7a-5250-411a-8bdd-01294bfa0a21', 'Tuck Reverse Crunch (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Cable Tuck Reverse Crunch, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2421201', '02421201-Cable-Tuck-Reverse-Crunch_waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Tuck Reverse Crunch. 2. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 3. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Tuck Reverse Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('eebeb4b2-eb1c-4b4a-a91f-e6883f173264', 'Cross Lat Pulldown (Machine, Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this pulling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '71791201', '71791201-Lever-Cross-Lat-Pulldown-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Cross Lat Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Cross Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('eeccfe99-cbb6-47a7-b4f0-2b9a8ee2df52', 'Pyramid Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Pyramid Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '58981201', '58981201-Pyramid-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Pyramid Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Pyramid Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eef1d447-a7c1-4e95-aa98-66c71072e4b4', 'Standing Rear Delt Row (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise works your rear delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '39761201', '39761201-Band-standing-rear-delt-row-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Rear Delt Row. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Standing Rear Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('eef3664c-2e9c-48a2-b47e-7cae36b6dcae', 'Incline Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Dumbbell Incline Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '11761201', '11761201-Dumbbell-Incline-Front-Raise_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Incline Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('eef85927-4309-41b5-8f2b-131248e9a7dd', 'Revolved Chair (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '58991201', '58991201-Revolved-Chair-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Move into the stretch position for Revolved Chair. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Revolved Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('eefdbc8e-3e34-4d70-a5d1-e2ede02a9fe7', 'Front To Under Knee Clap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '80331201', '80331201-Front-to-Under-Knee-Clap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Front To Under Knee Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Front To Under Knee Clap', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef002695-5479-42de-82b2-9e5438bfef14', 'Reverse Lunge With Overhead Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Reverse Lunge With Overhead Reach is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65511201', '65511201-Bodyweight-Reverse-Lunge-with-Overhead-Reach-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Reverse Lunge With Overhead Reach', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef05bcf1-eba3-47eb-889d-3ad79a013e40', 'Ring Front Lever (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '75141201', '75141201-Ring-Front-Lever-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Ring Front Lever. 2. Set up in the starting position for Ring Front Lever. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_lever', 'Ring Front Lever', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ef12743f-f3de-4f93-82d9-5bb6ee4ae1a3', 'Push Up (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Lever Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '69461201', '69461201-Lever-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Lever Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ef138762-6ae1-4c27-9b06-9f7c56a6e13e', 'Front Leg Swing (Wall Supported)', 'Full Body', 'Wall', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '93531201', '93531201-Wall-Supported-Front-Leg-Swing-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Wall Supported Front Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef1ef704-ec9c-456b-bba1-e103ec99ebba', 'Seated Hamstring Side Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hamstrings, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '85631201', '85631201-Seated-Hamstring-Side-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Hamstring Side Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 30, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Seated Hamstring Side Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ef2c0521-ddde-41ee-bd53-f0eb31c9beb6', 'Lying Swimmer', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '78971201', '78971201-Lying-Swimmer-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Swimmer. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Swimmer. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'swimming', 'Lying Swimmer', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef2fd52e-92d1-4102-93e5-94686d091cc9', 'Standing Side Kick', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Side Kick is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic kicking movements. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66701201', '66701201-Standing-Side-Kick-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Side Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Side Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef39e6d2-6a5f-4564-aff5-9d6c6ed804a4', 'Assisted Chin Up Low Bar Position (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '47161201', '47161201-Assisted-Chin-up-(low-bar-position)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Assisted Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef4179df-4b3d-4a57-b76f-6c043b41e00e', 'Pullover (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your lats, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '43391201', '43391201-Barbell-Pullover_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ef45392a-e01c-47b1-bacb-141cffde894a', 'Cat Cow Circle', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Cat Cow Circle provides a deep stretch for your spine, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78961201', '78961201-Cat-Cow-Circle-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cat Cow Circle. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cat Cow Circle', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef4906ab-2e67-4255-82f5-898346af9f1e', 'Kneeling Single Kickback Fire Hydrant', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. You''ll also feel your hip abductors working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '73751201', '73751201-Kneeling-Single-Kickback-Fire-Hydrant-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Kneeling Single Kickback Fire Hydrant', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef5085f8-573b-477d-80a9-eb8b32c06c5e', 'Step (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '57471201', '57471201-Lever-Step-(female)-(VERSION-2)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Step. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lever Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ef574279-c2d5-4ec6-b349-0ec4e785b5d9', 'Walking Knee Raise Sky Reach On Spot', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Walking Knee Raise Sky Reach On Spot (front Pov) ( is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '96421201', '96421201-Walking-Knee-Raise-Sky-Reach-On-Spot-(front-POV)-(.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Walking Knee Raise Sky Reach On Spot  (', 'Walking Knee Raise Sky Reach On Spot (', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ef6f1d52-8fa7-47d2-b857-747d85c19ddf', 'Seated Calf Raise (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '881201', '00881201-Barbell-Seated-Calf-Raise_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Seated Calf Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Push', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Unilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, 'Overhand', 'Standard', 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Seated Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, standing_calf_raise', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95);
